# Own-wording spell text for Spells That Don't Suck (Ben Somers, somanyrobots), via Open5e. CC-BY 4.0.
TEXT = {'Adaptation': ['Level 2. Touch a creature to give it one environmental trait for 1 hour: gills, a gliding membrane, a prehensile tail, a changeable appearance, or a natural weapon.',
                'The target picks one adaptation and can swap it for another as an action. Casting the spell again or dismissing it ends it. Aquatic: breathe underwater and swim at walking speed. '
                'Glider: as a reaction when falling, reduce the fall by up to 100 ft and glide horizontally up to its walking speed. Prehensile tail: 5 ft reach, can carry five times the Strength '
                'score in pounds, and can grasp, lift, push, pull, open things, grapple or make unarmed strikes. Shapeshifter: as an action change height, weight, face, voice, hair and marks, but '
                'not size or limb count. Natural weapon: unarmed strikes with it deal 1d6 bludgeoning, piercing or slashing, are magical and get +1 to attack and damage. Higher slots: +2 weapon '
                'bonus at slot 4+, +3 at slot 6+, and the target may hold one more adaptation for every two slot levels above 2nd.'],
 'Alter Weather': ['Level 6. Shift precipitation, temperature and wind each by one stage in a 1-mile radius. Changes take 30 minutes to settle.',
                   'You need a clear view of the sky, and the spell ends if you finish a turn unable to see it. When cast you may move each of the three scales one stage, and you can move them again '
                   'later (30 minutes to take effect). Precipitation: 1 clear, 2 light clouds, 3 overcast or fog (no sunlight), 4 rain, hail or snow (lightly obscured past 60 ft), 5 torrential '
                   '(heavily obscured past 30 ft, difficult terrain). Temperature: 1 unbearable heat (DC 10 Con save each hour or gain exhaustion), 2 hot (disadvantage on Con saves except against '
                   'weather), 3 warm, 4 pleasant, 5 cool, 6 cold (disadvantage on Dex checks), 7 bitter cold (as stage 1). Wind: 1 calm, 2 moderate, 3 strong (disadvantage on ranged attacks), 4 gale '
                   '(resistance to ranged damage), 5 hurricane (no ranged attacks, movement against the wind costs double). Higher stages include lower ones. The GM may let gear protect creatures. '
                   'When it ends, weather returns at the same pace. Higher slots: 7th 8 hours and 5-mile radius, 8th 24 hours and 10 miles, 9th 7 days and 25 miles.'],
 'Animal Ally': ['Level 2. Link minds with a friendly beast. It can use your proficiency on checks, adds 1d6 damage, and gets advantage against your recent targets.',
                 'Choose a friendly beast in range. As an action you can use its senses until the start of your next turn. While it is within 120 ft you can speak to each other telepathically, and '
                 'the beast adds your proficiency bonus to its ability checks, deals an extra 1d6 damage on each hit, and has advantage on attacks against any creature you attacked since the start '
                 'of your last turn. Higher slots: duration 8 hours at slot 4+, 24 hours at slot 6+.'],
 'Animal Transformation': ['Level 4. Turn a creature into a beast of CR up to its own level or CR, max 4. Charisma save if unwilling.',
                           'Fails on a creature at 0 hit points. An unwilling target makes a Charisma save and repeats it at the end of each of its turns. The new form is a beast whose CR is at most '
                           "the target's CR or level, never above 4. The target takes the beast's statistics but keeps alignment, personality and allegiances, and gains the form's hit points. "
                           'Reverting restores the old hit points, and leftover damage from dropping to 0 carries over. It cannot speak, cast spells or use hands. Its gear melds into the form and '
                           'cannot be used. Ends when the target hits 0 hit points. Higher slots: maximum CR rises by 1 per slot level above 4th.'],
 'Arcane Shelter': ['Level 3. Raise a 10 ft radius dome for 8 hours that shelters ten Medium creatures and blocks projectiles and spells.',
                    'Casting takes 1 minute. The stationary dome is centered on you and vanishes if you leave it. It fails if there is not enough room. Ten Medium creatures fit (a Large one counts '
                    'as four). Up to ten creatures you name can pass through, spending 25 ft of movement to do so. Others cannot enter. The dome is translucent, stops projectiles, and blocks spells '
                    'and magical effects from passing or being cast through it.'],
 'Arcane Wall': ['Level 5. Create an invisible wall of force: panels, dome or sphere. AC 15, 100 hit points per panel, immune to dispel magic.',
                 'Place an invisible wall in any orientation, free-floating or resting on a surface. Shape it as a sphere or hemisphere up to 10 ft radius, or a flat surface of up to ten 10 ft by 10 '
                 'ft panels, each touching another. It is 1/4 inch thick. Creatures in its way are pushed to a side you choose. Nothing passes through it. Each panel has AC 15 and 100 hit points. It '
                 'is immune to psychic and nonmagical weapon damage and cannot be dispelled, but disintegrate destroys it. It extends into the Ethereal Plane and blocks travel there.'],
 "Arcanist's Sword": ['Level 7. A force blade acts on bonus-action commands: attack for 3d10 + modifier, guard an ally, or whirl for 3d10 area damage.',
                      'A glowing sword of force hovers in range for the duration. When it appears, and as a bonus action each turn, give it one command. Attack: it moves up to 20 ft and makes a '
                      "melee spell attack, dealing 3d10 force plus your spellcasting modifier on a hit. Guard: it moves up to 20 ft into a creature's space and gives it half cover. The first time a "
                      'hostile creature comes within 5 ft of it, it makes a melee spell attack for the same damage and cannot attack again until commanded. Whirl: it moves up to 20 ft to a point and '
                      'spins. A creature that starts in its space or passes within 5 ft on its turn makes a Dexterity save or takes 3d10 force damage.'],
 'Arctic Breath': ['Level 1. A 30 ft line of freezing wind. Dex save: 2d8 cold and -10 ft speed, half and no slow on success.',
                   'A line 30 ft long and 5 ft wide blasts from you. Each creature in it makes a Dexterity save. On a failure it takes 2d8 cold damage and its speed drops by 10 ft until the end of '
                   'its next turn. On a success it takes half damage and is not slowed. Higher slots: +1d8 damage per slot level above 1st.'],
 'Assemble': ['Level 4. Turn raw or partly worked materials in range into up to eight nonmagical objects, as eight hours of crafting.',
              'Casting takes 1 minute. Target unfinished, unattended materials you can see (raw ore, felled trees, boards, ingots, canvas, silk, wool, flax, hemp, stone). You make up to eight '
              'objects: a Large object counts as eight, Medium or Small as one, Tiny as one-eighth. Objects cannot be firmly attached to a surface or larger object, and metal or stone products are '
              "at most Medium. Finished goods, creatures and magic items are unaffected. You need proficiency with the matching artisan's tools for items of fitting quality. The spell counts as "
              'eight hours of work, which can be part of a longer project.'],
 'Aura of Concealment': ['Level 2. A 30 ft aura gives you and chosen allies +5 to Stealth and leaves no trace to track.',
                         'You radiate magic in a 30 ft aura. While it lasts, you or a creature you choose in the aura gains +5 on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. Chosen creatures leave no trail and can '
                         'only be tracked by magic. Higher slots: the bonus rises by 1 per slot level above 2nd. Design note: group Stealth checks should be run against passive Perception as '
                         'written.'],
 'Aura of Truth': ['Level 2. A 15 ft aura. First time a creature ends its turn in it, Charisma save or it cannot lie. You may force answers once.',
                   'The aura moves with you. The first time a creature ends its turn inside, it makes a Charisma save. On a failure it cannot intentionally lie while in the aura. A creature may '
                   'choose to fail, and you know the result. Affected creatures know of the spell and may answer evasively. As an action you can compel answers: ask up to two yes-or-no questions, '
                   'each to an affected creature, which must answer truthfully. The spell then ends. Higher slots: radius +5 ft and +1 question per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Beast Perception': ['Level 2. Choose one animal sense: darkvision 30, echolocation, keen hearing, sight or smell, tremorsense 30, or websense. Swap as an action.',
                      'Pick one option. You can end it as an action to take another. Darkvision 30 ft. Echolocation: blindsight 10 ft while you keep making high-pitched sounds, so you cannot speak '
                      'normally, and the squeaks carry 60 ft. Keen Hearing, Keen Sight or Keen Smell: advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks using that sense. Tremorsense 30 ft. Websense: while '
                      'touching a web, you know the exact position of any creature touching the same web.'],
 'Befriend': ['Cantrip. Advantage on Persuasion or Deception against one creature for 10 minutes, then it turns hostile.',
              'Casting takes 1 minute. One creature you can see in range is compelled to like and trust you. You have advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) or Charisma (Deception) checks against it. '
              'When the spell ends the target knows you influenced it and becomes hostile. A violent creature may attack, others may spread word, call guards or work against you.'],
 'Befriend Beast': ['Level 1. A beast (Int 3 or less) makes a Wisdom save or is charmed 1 hour and will scout, fetch or carry messages.',
                    'Choose a beast you can see that can see and hear you. It makes a Wisdom save or is charmed for the duration. Beasts with Intelligence 4 or higher succeed automatically. The '
                    'spell ends if you or your companions harm it. While charmed it performs simple tasks such as scouting, finding or delivering. It understands places and general descriptions but '
                    'cannot reliably find a specific person. It covers about 1 mile an hour walking, 2 if flying. Higher slots: slot 2 lasts 24 hours. Slot 3+: add 24 hours per slot level above 2nd, '
                    'or affect one more beast per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Benediction': ['Cantrip. A blessing lets a creature add 1d4 to one ability check of its choice.',
                 'Casting takes 1 minute. Target a creature in range that can see and understand you. Once before the spell ends, it can roll 1d4 and add it to one ability check, before or after '
                 'rolling. The spell then ends. A creature with Intelligence 4 or higher that sees the casting knows magic influenced it. Design note: only the largest bonus-die effect should apply '
                 'to a d20 roll.'],
 'Bewilder': ['Level 4. 20 ft sphere. Wisdom save or no reactions, half movement in a random direction, and a d4 table of odd behavior each turn.',
              'Each creature in a 20 ft radius sphere makes a Wisdom save when you cast. Affected targets cannot take reactions. At the start of each of its turns a target spends half its movement '
              'moving in a random horizontal direction (roll d8), then rolls d4: 1 stunned until its next turn, 2 treats everyone as an enemy until its next turn, 3 frightened of everyone it sees '
              'until its next turn, 4 drops what it holds and does nothing this turn. At the end of each turn, or whenever it takes damage, a target repeats the save and ends the effect on a '
              'success. Higher slots: +5 ft radius per slot level above 4th.'],
 'Black Ice': ['Cantrip. A 5 ft square of ice for 1 minute. Dex save: 1d6 cold, and prone if Medium or smaller.',
               'Make a patch of clear ice on ground you see. Any creature in the space when cast makes a Dexterity save or takes 1d6 cold damage, and falls prone if Medium or smaller. A creature '
               'repeats the save the first time each turn it enters the ice and when it ends a turn on it. Damage rises to 2d6 at level 5, 3d6 at 11 and 4d6 at 17.'],
 'Blade Burst': ['Cantrip. Blades hit all other creatures within 5 ft: Dex save or 1d6 slashing or piercing (your choice).',
                 'A ring of blades slashes at foes around you. Every other creature within 5 ft makes a Dexterity save or takes 1d6 slashing or piercing damage, your choice. Damage rises to 2d6 at '
                 'level 5, 3d6 at 11 and 4d6 at 17.'],
 'Blazing Blade': ['Level 5. Bonus action. A touched weapon gains +1d6 fire and +1d6 radiant, and can unleash a 30 ft cone of holy fire once.',
                   'Touch a weapon. For the duration it deals an extra 1d6 fire and 1d6 radiant damage on a hit, and its base damage type becomes fire or radiant, your choice. Sunfire Swipe: the '
                   'wielder can use a bonus action to release a 30 ft cone, ending the spell. Each creature in it makes a Dexterity save (disadvantage for undead and fiends). On a failure it takes '
                   '3d6 fire and 3d6 radiant damage and is afflicted by holy fire for 1 minute: attacks against it have advantage if the attacker sees it, and it gets no benefit from being '
                   'invisible. On a success it takes half damage and no affliction. An afflicted creature repeats a Wisdom save at the end of each turn, ending it on a success. The weapon and any '
                   'afflicted creature shed bright light 30 ft and dim light 30 ft further.'],
 'Brilliance': ['Level 3. A 60 ft radius sphere of bright light (not sunlight) for 1 hour, which can ride on an object and dispels lesser darkness.',
                'A 60 ft radius sphere of light appears at a point in range, bright light with dim light 60 ft beyond. It is not sunlight. If you target a point on an object you hold, or one nobody '
                'wears or carries, the light comes from the object and moves with it. Covering it fully with an opaque item blocks the light. Where it overlaps darkness made by a spell of its level '
                'or lower (or a similar effect), that darkness is dispelled.'],
 'Burst of Flame': ['Level 2. A fiery blast at a point within 60 ft. Choose light (blinds), heat (3d6 fire) or smoke (15 ft cloud). Stronger on an existing flame.',
                    'Pick one effect. Using an existing nonmagical flame as the center puts out up to a 5 ft cube of it and strengthens the effect. Light: creatures in a 10 ft radius make a '
                    'Constitution save or are blinded until the end of your next turn (20 ft radius on a flame). Heat: creatures in a 10 ft radius make a Constitution save, taking 3d6 fire on a '
                    'failure or half on a success (4d6 on a flame). Smoke: a 15 ft radius cloud of thick oily smoke that spreads around corners and heavily obscures its area (30 ft radius on a '
                    'flame), lasting 1 minute or until a strong breeze scatters it.'],
 'Call for Aid': ['Level 6. A powerful extraplanar being sends a loyal servant who may help, for a price (about 50 gp a minute).',
                  'Casting takes 1 minute. You appeal to a god, archdevil or other mighty extraplanar being, which sends a loyal servant to an open space in range. It is friendly but not obliged to '
                  'help, and speaks at least one language you know. It usually demands payment suited to its nature (tithes for a celestial, sacrifices for a fiend). Monetary payment is typically 50 '
                  'gp per minute, 500 gp per hour or 5,000 gp per day, adjusted up to 50 percent by how much the being backs the task or how dangerous it is. Repeated calls cost more, and the first '
                  'may be free if the being favors you. It does tasks fitting its nature and rarely accepts suicidal, impossible, abhorrent or very long ones. After finishing, or if you cannot pay, '
                  'it returns home.'],
 'Captivate': ['Level 2. A performance charms chosen creatures (Wisdom save): they ignore everyone but you and are slowed when initiative is rolled.',
               'Creatures you choose in range make a Wisdom save or are charmed by you. Creatures fighting you or your companions have advantage. A charmed creature has disadvantage on initiative '
               'and on Wisdom (Perception) checks to notice anyone other than you, until the spell ends or it can no longer see or hear you. If it rolls initiative while affected, its speed drops by '
               '10 ft and it cannot take reactions until after its first turn. The spell ends if you are incapacitated or cannot speak. Creatures that fail do not realize you used magic. Higher '
               'slots: +1 minute and +10 ft radius per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Caustic Quarrel': ['Level 2. Ranged spell attack: 6d4 acid, and the target keeps burning for 4d4 more unless it wipes the acid off.',
                     'Make a ranged spell attack against a target in range. On a hit it takes 6d4 acid damage and is coated in acid. The target can use its action to wipe it off. If it does not, it '
                     'takes another 4d4 acid damage at the end of its next turn. Higher slots: both damage amounts rise by 1d4 per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Circle of Protection': ['Level 3. A 10 ft glyph and 30 ft tall cylinder bars one creature type of CR 5 or lower. Charisma save to act across it.',
                          'Draw a 10 ft radius glyph that rises into a luminous 30 ft cylinder. Choose aberrations, celestials, elementals, fey, fiends or undead. A creature of that type with CR 5 '
                          'or lower cannot willingly cross the boundary. If it tries to attack, cast, teleport, travel between planes or cause any effect across it, it must first succeed on a '
                          'Charisma save. When you start casting you can make it non-concentration, which makes that casting take 10 minutes. Higher slots: maximum CR rises by 3 per slot level above '
                          '3rd. Slots 5 and 6: concentration up to 12 hours. Slots 7 and 8: concentration up to 24 hours. Slot 9: lasts until dispelled with no CR limit.'],
 'Cold Snap': ['Level 2. 5 ft radius burst at a point within 90 ft. Con save: 3d8 cold and -10 ft speed, plus icy difficult terrain.',
               'A burst of freezing wind erupts at a point in range. Each creature in a 5 ft radius sphere makes a Constitution save. On a failure it takes 3d8 cold damage and its speed is cut by 10 '
               'ft until the start of your next turn. On a success it takes half damage and is not slowed. The area becomes slick ice and snow, difficult terrain until the start of your next turn. '
               'Higher slots: +1d8 damage per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Command Beast': ['Level 3. Wisdom save or a beast (CR under 4) is charmed 1 minute. Give telepathic orders, or take full control as an action.',
                   'A beast you can see in range makes a Wisdom save or is charmed for the duration. A beast of CR 4 or higher succeeds automatically, and it has advantage if you or your friends are '
                   'fighting it. While charmed you can give it telepathic commands at no action cost while conscious, and it does its best to obey simple general orders. After finishing an order it '
                   'defends itself. As an action you can take full control until the end of your next turn: it takes only the actions you choose, and its reactions cost your reaction. Each time it '
                   'takes damage it repeats the save, ending the spell on a success. Higher slots: slot 4+ removes the CR limit.'],
 'Command Objects': ['Level 5. Animate up to six same-size objects as allies that attack on bonus-action commands, using your spell attack bonus.',
                     'Choose up to six unattended nonmagical objects in range, all the same size: six Tiny, four Small, three Medium, two Large or one Huge. Each stays animate until the spell ends '
                     'or it drops to 0 hit points (extra damage carries to the original object). Statistics by size. Tiny: 5 HP, AC 19, Str 12, Dex 28, 1d4+1 damage, fly 30 (hover). Small: 10 HP, AC '
                     '18, Str 16, Dex 24, 1d6+3, fly 30. Medium: 20 HP, AC 17, Str 20, Dex 20, 1d10+5, speed 30. Large: 30 HP, AC 16, Str 24, Dex 16, 2d10+7, speed 25. Huge: 60 HP, AC 15, Str 28, '
                     'Dex 12, 5d12+9, speed 20. Each has blindsight 30 ft. The GM may add resistances or vulnerabilities from its form. An object fixed to a surface or larger object has speed 0. '
                     'Objects share your initiative and act right after you. As a bonus action you give one command to any number of them. Without orders they only Dodge. They can try grapple or '
                     'shove if their form allows. An attack order means one melee attack on a target within 5 ft, using your spell attack modifier, usually bludgeoning (the GM may rule slashing or '
                     'piercing).'],
 'Cone of Flame': ['Level 1. 15 ft cone. Dex save: 3d6 fire, half on success. Ignites loose flammables.',
                   'Flames spray from your fingertips. Each creature in a 15 ft cone makes a Dexterity save, taking 3d6 fire damage on a failure or half on a success. It lights unattended flammable '
                   'objects in the area. Higher slots: +1d6 damage and +5 ft cone length per slot level above 1st.'],
 'Confinement': ['Level 7. An invisible force cage or box (AC 17, 140 HP) traps creatures inside for 1 hour. Teleporting out needs a Charisma save.',
                 'An immobile invisible prison of force forms around an area in range, as a cage or a solid box. It has AC 17 and 140 hit points. A cage is up to 20 ft on a side, made of 1/2 inch '
                 'bars 1/2 inch apart, and gives half cover. A box is up to 10 ft on a side, a solid barrier blocking matter and spells in or out. Creatures fully inside are trapped. Creatures '
                 'partly inside or too large are pushed out. Nobody can leave by nonmagical means. A trapped creature using teleportation or planar travel to leave must first make a Charisma save, '
                 'succeeding to use the magic, otherwise it fails. It extends into the Ethereal Plane and cannot be dispelled by dispel magic. Higher slots: +1 AC and +20 hit points per slot level '
                 'above 7th.'],
 'Conjure Beast Pack': ['Level 3. Summon eight Small or Tiny beasts of CR 1/4 or less (six if flying). They hit as a pack for 1d4 each plus 1d4 per extra attacker.',
                        'Choose a Small or Tiny beast of CR 1/4 or lower. Eight of that type appear around you (six if it flies). They count as fey, vanish at 0 hit points or when the spell ends, '
                        'and are friendly to you and companions. They share your initiative, taking turns after yours, and obey verbal commands without using your action. Without orders they move as '
                        'a group and Dodge. When ordered to attack, assign each beast a target within its reach and make one melee spell attack per target. On a hit the target takes 1d4 bludgeoning '
                        'or piercing (your choice) plus 1d4 for each additional beast attacking it. You have advantage if three or more beasts attack one target, and you add your spellcasting '
                        'modifier to damage if six or more do. The beasts do not use their normal attacks. Higher slots: two more beasts per slot level above 3rd.'],
 'Conjure Herald': ['Level 2. A ghostly herald delivers a 25-word message: fixed at a place until a trigger (ward), or roaming 5 miles for 1 hour (announcement).',
                    'Casting takes 1 minute. You create a Medium or Small ghostly spirit of any look that knows a fixed message of up to 25 words. Choose an effect. Ward: it is set at a location, or '
                    "on a statue or object with a mouth, and stays invisible and still until a condition you set is met within 30 ft. Then it appears and recites the message (moving the object's "
                    'mouth if on an object). You decide whether it does this once or repeats whenever triggered. A ward lasts until dispelled. Announcement: it floats up to 100 ft up and 30 ft per '
                    'round, repeating the message each round across a 5-mile radius around the spot, telling every creature it sees. It lasts 1 hour.'],
 'Conjure Minor Fiends': ['Level 3. Summon two demons (Minor Fiend stats) or fiends totaling CR 2. If you lose concentration they turn on you and stay.',
                          'You may pick the plane they come from. The spell conjures two demons using the Minor Fiend block, or the GM picks fiends with total CR 2 or lower. They share your '
                          'initiative, going after you, and are friendly to you and companions, hostile to everyone else. If you lose concentration they do not vanish: they turn hostile to you and '
                          'your companions, cannot be dismissed, and last 1 hour from summoning. A fiend disappears at 0 hit points. Minor Fiend: Medium fiend (demon), AC 14, 32 HP (5d8+10), speed '
                          '30. Str 16, Dex 14, Con 16, Int 8, Wis 14, Cha 8. Resists cold, fire, lightning. Immune to poison, charmed, frightened, poisoned. Darkvision 60, passive Perception 12, '
                          'speaks Abyssal or Infernal and understands one language you speak. CR 1. Magic Resistance: advantage on saves against spells and magic. Multiattack: two attacks, only one '
                          'Abyssal Bile. Claws: +5 to hit, reach 5, 1d8+3 slashing. Abyssal Bile: one creature within 10 ft makes a Charisma save against your spell save DC. On a failure roll d4: 1 '
                          'frightened of the fiend, 2 poisoned, 3 restrained, 4 burns for 1d6 fire at the start of each of its turns. It repeats the save at the end of each turn, ending the effect '
                          'on a success. After a successful save it is immune to the ability for 24 hours. Higher slots: +1 fiend or +1 total CR per slot level above 3rd.'],
 'Corpse Puppets': ['Level 5. Raise up to five Tiny to Medium corpses as skeleton or zombie puppets under your command (bonus action).',
                    'Your shadow splits and reanimates up to five Tiny, Small or Medium corpses of CR 1/4 or higher you can see in range. Each becomes an undead of its size as a Skeleton or Zombie '
                    'of your choice. They are allies, share your initiative and act after you. As a bonus action you command any number of puppets in range. Without orders they Dodge and avoid '
                    'danger. They obey until the spell ends, then become inanimate. Skeleton: AC 13, 15 HP, speed 35, Str 12 Dex 16 Con 12 Int 6 Wis 8 Cha 5, vulnerable to bludgeoning, CR 1/2. '
                    'Multiattack: two Skeletal Slash (your spell attack modifier, reach 5, 1d6+1 slashing). Zombie: AC 8, 25 HP, speed 20, Str 14 Dex 6 Con 16 Int 6 Wis 8 Cha 5. Both immune to '
                    'poison, exhaustion and poisoned, darkvision 60, passive Perception 9, understand but cannot speak. Festering Fortitude (Zombie): at 0 HP, make a Con save (DC = damage taken) '
                    'unless the damage is radiant or a critical hit, and drop to 1 HP on a success. Seizing Swarm (Zombie): advantage to grapple a creature if another conscious allied Zombie Puppet '
                    'is within 5 ft of it. Body Bash (Zombie): your spell attack modifier, reach 5, 2d4+2 bludgeoning. Higher slots: two more corpses per slot level above 5th.'],
 'Corrosive Burst': ['Level 4. 20 ft acid explosion at a point within 150 ft. Dex save: 8d4 acid, half on success, plus 4d4 each turn until cleaned.',
                     'You hurl a ball of acid that bursts in a 20 ft radius sphere at a point you see in range. Each creature in it makes a Dexterity save, taking 8d4 acid on a failure or half on a '
                     'success. A creature that fails takes 4d4 more acid at the end of each of its turns until it or another creature within 5 ft uses an action to clear the acid. Higher slots: '
                     'initial damage +2d4 per slot level above 4th.'],
 'Curse of Weakness': ['Level 2. A 10 ft radius zone. Con save each turn in it or be weakened: disadvantage on Strength checks and saves, half Strength weapon damage, -10 speed.',
                       'Ghastly energy fills a 10 ft radius sphere centered on a point in range. A creature that starts its turn there or moves in during its turn makes a Constitution save. On a '
                       'failure it is cursed until the end of its turn: disadvantage on Strength checks and Strength saves, half damage from Strength-based weapon attacks, and speed reduced by 10 '
                       'ft. Higher slots: +5 ft radius per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Dazzle': ['Level 1. 20 ft cone of glittering motes. Con save or blinded and half speed until the end of your next turn.',
            'Each creature in a 20 ft cone sees your space as heavily obscured and makes a Constitution save. On a failure it is blinded and its speed is halved. The spell ends at the end of your '
            'next turn. Higher slots: +5 ft cone per slot level above 1st.'],
 'Death Ray': ['Level 7. Ranged spell attack: 8d10+30 necrotic, half on a miss. A humanoid that dies rises as a zombie.',
               'Make a ranged spell attack against a creature in range. On a hit it takes 8d10+30 necrotic damage, on a miss half. A humanoid killed by the spell, or dying within 1 minute of being '
               'hit, rises as a zombie at the start of your next turn and attacks the closest living creature (basic zombie statistics or the reanimation template; the GM may allow other undead for '
               'other creature types). Higher slots: +2d10 damage per slot level above 7th.'],
 'Deflect': ['Level 1. Reaction. +5 AC (max 21) until your next turn, including against the trigger, and magic missile cannot hurt you.',
             'A transparent sphere of force averts attacks. Until the start of your next turn you have +5 AC, to a maximum AC of 21, including against the triggering attack, and you take no damage '
             'from magic missile. Higher slots: the bonus and the AC maximum rise by 1 for every two slot levels above 1st (slot 5: +7, max 23).'],
 'Detect Hazards': ['Level 2. Sense traps within 120 ft (hidden pits, glyphs, sinkholes). Within 15 ft you pinpoint them and get advantage to examine them.',
                    'You sense any trap in range, meaning any object, terrain or magic that causes a sudden harmful effect: an alarm area, a glyph, a hidden pit or a natural sinkhole, but not an '
                    'ambush. You learn general presence and rough direction, not location. Within 15 ft of a trap you know its exact position, and checks you and companions make to examine it have '
                    'advantage. Blocked by 1 ft of stone, 1 inch of common metal, a thin sheet of lead, or 3 ft of wood or dirt.'],
 'Detect Otherworldly Influence': ['Level 1. Sense aberrations, celestials, elementals, fey, fiends and undead within 30 ft, with advantage on Perception and Insight against them.',
                                   'You learn the presence and location of aberrations, celestials, elementals, fey, fiends and undead within 30 ft, and have advantage on Wisdom (Perception) and '
                                   'Wisdom (Insight) checks against them. Blocked by 1 ft of stone, 1 inch of common metal, a thin sheet of lead, or 3 ft of wood or dirt.'],
 'Devil Binding': ['Level 5. Summon a devil of CR 4 to 8 (GM picks). It will not harm you and obeys reasonable orders, but may turn free after 10 minutes.',
                   'A profane chant brings a devil to an open space you see in range. Its CR is at least 4 and at most 8, and the GM chooses its type and controls it. Knowing its true name or '
                   'holding its talisman lets you try to summon that devil whatever its CR. It resents being summoned but will not harm you for the duration. You command it on your turns. It follows '
                   'reasonable orders and fights ruthlessly, but retreats to protect its life and rank. After 10 minutes it may ignore commands and stay for its own ends, and you can bargain or '
                   'reason with it. If you concentrate the whole duration you can send it home, otherwise it stays summoned. Higher slots: the possible CR rises by 2 per slot level above 5th.'],
 'Disrupting Smite': ['Level 5. Bonus action. Next melee hit adds 5d10 force. Charisma save or the target is phased out: incapacitated with resistance to all damage.',
                      'Your weapon tears the fabric of the planes. The next time you hit with a melee weapon attack before the spell ends, the hit deals 5d10 extra force damage, and the target makes '
                      'a Charisma save. On a failure it is partly phased out: incapacitated and resistant to all damage until the spell ends. It repeats the Charisma save at the end of each of its '
                      'turns, ending the spell on a success.'],
 'Divine Temple': ['Level 6. Casting 1 hour. Create a 60 ft temple for 24 hours that blocks low-level divination and repels chosen creature types.',
                   'You make a holy sanctuary at an empty ground point in range, a cube up to 60 ft on a side with a door and enclosed by wood and stone floors, walls and roof. You decide its look '
                   '(altars, idols, light, rooms, scent, temperature, windows) as long as it suits the deity of the holy symbol you used. Divination spells of 6th level or lower cannot target '
                   'creatures inside or create sensors in it. Choose one or more types to oppose: aberrations, celestials, elementals, fey, fiends, undead. Such a creature trying to enter makes a '
                   'Charisma save, failing it cannot enter for 24 hours. On a success, each attack roll, ability check and saving throw it makes inside takes -1d4. Casting it on the same spot daily '
                   'for a year makes the effect permanent. Higher slots: +1 hour casting time and +60 ft per side per slot level above 6th, and it counters divinations of up to the slot level used.'],
 'Draining Bolt': ['Cantrip. Ranged spell attack: 1d6 necrotic, and the target has disadvantage on its next weapon attack until the end of its next turn.',
                   'Make a ranged spell attack against a creature you see in range. On a hit it takes 1d6 necrotic damage and has disadvantage on the next weapon attack roll it makes before the end '
                   'of its next turn. Damage rises to 2d6 at level 5, 3d6 at 11 and 4d6 at 17.'],
 'Drink Life': ['Level 5. A tendril drains a creature: Con save, 6d8 necrotic and half speed. You heal half the damage. Repeat each turn.',
                'A black tendril reaches one creature you see in range, which makes a Constitution save. On a failure it takes 6d8 necrotic damage and its speed is halved until the start of your '
                'next turn. On a success it takes half and nothing else. You regain hit points equal to half the damage dealt. Until the spell ends, you can use your action each turn to repeat the '
                'effect on a creature in range. Higher slots: +1d8 damage per slot level above 5th.'],
 'Dust Cyclone': ['Level 2. A 5 ft radius, 30 ft tall cyclone you can move 30 ft as a bonus action. Str save: 1d12 bludgeoning and pushed 5 ft.',
                  'A small cyclone rises at a ground point you see in range, a cylinder 5 ft in radius and 30 ft high. A creature that starts its turn in it or enters its radius for the first time '
                  'on a turn makes a Strength save. On a failure it takes 1d12 bludgeoning and is pushed 5 ft from the center, on a success half damage and no push. As a bonus action you move it up '
                  'to 30 ft. The first time you pass it through a creature you can force the save as if it had entered. After that its force is spent until the end of your turn. Over sand, dust, '
                  'loose dirt or gravel it draws up material and heavily obscures its radius until the start of your next turn.'],
 'Earth Forming': ['Level 5. For the duration, reshape up to a 20 ft cube of soft earth per action, permanently, moving it up to 20 ft over 5 minutes.',
                   'As an action you permanently modify up to a 20 ft cube of soft earth (sand, dirt, clay) you see in range, shifting it up to 20 ft over 5 minutes. You can change elevation, or '
                   'create or remove trenches, pillars, ramps, walls and other simple shapes. The change is slow, so creatures are not normally trapped or hurt. You can pick a new area at any time '
                   'but shape only one at a time, and an unfinished shape slowly reverts. It cannot shape stone, metal or other hard material. Rocks, plants and structures shift to fit and may '
                   'become unstable or fall. Cast as a ritual, the silver pickaxe must be worth at least 500 gp and is consumed.'],
 'Earth Leash': ['Level 2. Strength save or fall prone. A flier loses its fly speed for the duration and falls (up to 4d6 fall damage).',
                 'A tendril of earth hauls one creature you see in range to the ground. It makes a Strength save or falls prone. If it has a flying speed, it loses it for the duration and falls even '
                 'if it can hover, taking normal falling damage up to 4d6 bludgeoning. Higher slots: +1 target and +1d6 maximum fall damage per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Earth Rumble': ['Level 1. 10 ft radius around you. Dex save: 2d6 bludgeoning and prone. Dirt or stone becomes difficult terrain for 1 hour.',
                  'The ground around you shakes. Each other creature within 10 ft makes a Dexterity save. On a failure it takes 2d6 bludgeoning and is knocked prone, on a success half damage and not '
                  'prone. Dirt or stone in the area becomes difficult terrain for everyone but you for 1 hour. Higher slots: +1d6 damage per slot level above 1st and +5 ft radius for every two slot '
                  'levels above 1st.'],
 'Eldritch Armor': ['Level 1. Gain 1d4+4 temporary hit points. While you have them, melee attackers take 2d4 acid.',
                    'You coat yourself in acid that sprays when struck. You gain 1d4+4 temporary hit points for the duration. If a creature hits you with a melee attack while you have them, it takes '
                    '2d4 acid damage. Higher slots: both the temporary hit points and the acid damage rise by 2d4 per slot level above 1st, to at most 9d4+4 temporary hit points and 10d4 damage at '
                    'slot 5.'],
 'Eldritch Rift': ['Level 1. 10 ft radius around you. Str save: 3d4 necrotic and no reactions until your next turn, otherwise disadvantage on opportunity attacks.',
                   'You open a brief portal to a void and tentacles tear at nearby foes. Each other creature within 10 ft makes a Strength save. On a failure it takes 3d4 necrotic damage and is '
                   'gripped, unable to take reactions until the start of its next turn. On a success it takes half and has disadvantage on opportunity attacks until the start of its next turn. '
                   'Higher slots: +2d4 damage per slot level above 1st, and the radius can grow by up to 5 ft per slot level above 1st.'],
 'Elemental Reflection': ['Level 1. Reaction. Resist the triggering damage, then either extend it a round or add 1d8 of that type plus a rider to your next weapon attack.',
                          'An elemental ward gives you resistance to the triggering damage. When you cast it, choose to extend the resistance until the end of your next turn, or have your next '
                          "weapon attack before then deal an extra 1d8 damage of the triggering type with an effect. Acid: the target takes 1d4 acid at the end of its next turn. Cold: the target's "
                          'speed is cut by 10 ft until the end of your next turn. Fire: the attack ignites unattended flammable objects. Lightning: the target cannot take reactions until the start '
                          'of its next turn. Thunder: the target is deafened until the end of its next turn. Higher slots: +1d8 extra damage per slot level above 1st.'],
 'Elemental Shield': ['Level 6. Immunity to one chosen damage type (acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder) and resistance to it for creatures within 5 ft. Change type as a bonus action.',
                      'Choose acid, cold, fire, lightning or thunder. For the duration you are immune to that damage type, and creatures you choose within 5 ft of you have resistance to it. As a '
                      "bonus action you can change the shield's damage type."],
 'Enkindle': ['Level 2. Bonus action. Heat a Medium or smaller unworn object: a holder makes Con saves for 2d4 fire and disadvantage using it. Held to the end, it is destroyed.',
              'Choose a Medium or smaller object nobody wears, in range. It heats rapidly: metal or non-flammable things glow white-hot, flammable things catch fire without being destroyed. A '
              'creature holding it makes a Constitution save at the start of each of its turns, taking 2d4 fire damage and having disadvantage on ability checks and attacks using the item on a '
              'failure, or half damage and no other effect on a success. If you keep concentrating for the whole minute, a nonmagical item is melted, burned to ash or otherwise destroyed. Higher '
              'slots: +1d4 fire per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Erudition': ['Level 3. Gain proficiency in a chosen skill, expertise if already proficient, or reroll a die when you already have expertise and advantage. 1 hour.',
               'You call on legendary knowledge. Choose a skill. You gain proficiency in it. If you were already proficient you gain expertise (double proficiency bonus on checks with it). If you '
               'already have expertise, whenever you have advantage on that check you can reroll one of the dice once. The spell ends early if you cast it again.'],
 'Ethereal Slip': ['Level 3. Blink-style spell: at the end of each turn roll d20, on 11+ you slip into the Ethereal Plane until your next turn, with the roll rigged by your last result.',
                   'At the end of each of your turns roll a d20. On 11 or higher you slip into the Ethereal Plane and return at the start of your next turn in the space you left (or the nearest open '
                   'space). If your previous roll was 11 or higher, roll 2d20 and take the lower. If it was 10 or lower, roll 2d20 and take the higher. On the Ethereal Plane only creatures that can '
                   'see it can perceive you. You see and hear your home plane out to 60 ft but cannot interact with or affect anything there. When the spell ends you return to your plane. You cannot '
                   'cast it while already on the Ethereal Plane.'],
 'Expose Weakness': ['Level 4. Bonus action. Pick a target and a non-weapon damage type. Charisma save or lose resistance, and take +2d6 of that type from the first two hits each round.',
                     'Choose a creature you see in range and a damage type other than bludgeoning, piercing or slashing. The target makes a Charisma save or loses any resistance to that type for the '
                     'duration. The first two times each round it takes that damage type, it takes an extra 2d6 of that type. Higher slots: one more instance each round for every two slot levels '
                     'above 4th.'],
 'Expulsion': ['Level 4. Charisma save or incapacitated with resistance to all damage. Extraplanar targets vanish on the second fail, banished home on the third, permanent if you concentrate fully.',
               'You brandish a repellent item at a creature you see in range. It makes a Charisma save or is partly wrenched off its plane: incapacitated and resistant to all damage for the '
               'duration. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on a success. A creature on its home plane just keeps saving. An extraplanar creature that fails a '
               'second save disappears from the plane entirely. If it fails a third, it is banished to its home plane and stops saving. If you keep concentration for the full duration, the '
               'banishment is permanent. A returning target reappears in its old space or the nearest open space. Higher slots: +1 target per slot level above 4th.'],
 'False Death': ['Level 3. Touch a willing creature: 10 temporary HP, and it can play dead (resist all but psychic, prone, aware) for 8 hours. Disease and poison are suppressed.',
                 'The target gains 10 temporary hit points for the duration. As an action, or as a reaction to being hit or taking damage, it can appear dead to inspection and to spells that check '
                 'its status, and its breathing is undetectable. In this state it falls prone, sees and hears normally, and has resistance to all damage except psychic. The state ends if it moves or '
                 'takes an action, bonus action or reaction, and then the spell ends. You can use an action to touch the target and dismiss the spell. Disease or poison the target has when cast, or '
                 'gets later, has no effect until the spell ends.'],
 'False Foes': ['Level 3. Intelligence save or the target treats everyone as an enemy and must use its reaction on any opportunity attack. Repeat the save on damage.',
                'The target makes an Intelligence save, succeeding automatically if immune to frightened. On a failure it treats every other creature as an enemy, fights with its normal tactics, and '
                'must use its reaction for an opportunity attack against any creature that provokes one. Each time it takes damage it repeats the save, ending the spell on a success.'],
 'Fated Strike': ["Level 1. Bonus action. A willing touched creature's next attack before the end of your next turn automatically hits.",
                  "You touch a willing creature and foretell an accurate strike. The next attack it makes before the end of your next turn hits regardless of modifiers or the target's AC. Higher "
                  'slots: one more automatic hit for every two slot levels above 1st.'],
 'Fearsome Visage': ['Level 1. Wisdom save or the target is frightened of you. Advantage on the save if over 90 ft away. Repeats each turn.',
                     'A creature in range makes a Wisdom save or is frightened of you for the duration. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success. A target '
                     'more than 90 ft away has advantage. Higher slots: +1 target per slot level above 1st.'],
 'Fiery Blade': ['Level 2. Bonus action. A fire scimitar in your free hand: 2d6 fire, finesse, light, thrown 20/60, lights targets for 1d6 per turn. Recall it as a bonus action.',
                 'The blade is the size of a scimitar and counts as a simple melee weapon you are proficient with. It sheds bright light 20 ft and dim light 20 ft further. It deals 2d6 fire damage '
                 'on a hit and has finesse, light and thrown (range 20/60). Hitting a flammable creature or object ignites it, dealing 1d6 fire at the start of each of its turns until a creature '
                 'uses an action to douse it. If you drop or throw the blade it fades at the end of the turn, but while the spell lasts you can use a bonus action to make it reappear in your hand. '
                 'Higher slots: blade and burning damage each +1d6 for every two slot levels above 2nd.'],
 'Fiery Quiver': ['Level 3. A touched quiver: ammunition from it adds 2d6 fire on a hit. One piece enchanted at a time, ending after six pieces.',
                  'You enchant a quiver for 10 minutes. Ammunition drawn from it deals an extra 2d6 fire damage on a hit. Only one piece of ammunition is affected at a time, and the spell ends after '
                  '6 pieces are used or if you cast it again. Higher slots: +1 piece per slot level above 3rd.'],
 'Find in Nature': ['Level 1. Name or describe a kind of beast or plant and learn the direction and distance to the nearest within 1 mile.',
                    'Locate a specific kind of beast or plant you name or describe. You learn the direction and distance to the closest one within 1 mile, if any. Higher slots: range 5 miles at slot '
                    '2, and +5 miles for each slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Fireblast': ['Level 3. A fire bead bursts in a 20 ft radius within 120 ft. Dex save: 7d6 fire, half on success. Spreads around corners.',
               'A marble-sized flame flies from your hand and explodes at a point in range. Each creature within 20 ft makes a Dexterity save, taking 7d6 fire damage on a failure or half on a '
               'success. The blast spreads around corners and ignites unattended flammable objects. Higher slots: +1d6 per slot level above 3rd.'],
 'Fleeting Portals': ['Level 6. Two linked 10 ft gates within 500 ft. You choose one- or two-way and can open, close or move them 60 ft as a bonus action.',
                      'Choose two unoccupied ground points you can see within 500 ft. A glowing 10 ft diameter gate opens at each. You decide whether the gates work from both sides or one. A '
                      'creature or object entering one exits the other as if adjacent. As a bonus action you can close, open or move one or both gates up to 60 ft. The spell ends if a gate moves '
                      'more than 500 ft from your original location.'],
 'Flickering Strikes': ['Level 5. Teleport to and strike up to five targets within 30 ft, each melee attack adding 6d6 force. End next to one of them.',
                        'Brandish the weapon you used to cast and vanish, instantly teleporting to and striking up to five targets in range. Make a melee weapon attack against each. On a hit a '
                        "target takes the weapon's damage plus 6d6 force. You then teleport to an open space you can see within 5 ft of any target."],
 'Force Weapon': ['Level 2. Bonus action. A touched weapon becomes magical with +1 to attack and +1d4 force damage, and can glow.',
                  'A nonmagical weapon becomes magical, gains +1 to attack rolls and deals an extra 1d4 force damage. The wielder can use a bonus action to start or stop it glowing, choosing the '
                  'color and bright light from a 5 ft to 30 ft radius, with equal dim light beyond. Higher slots: +2 and 1d6 at slot 4+, +3 and 1d8 at slot 6+.'],
 'Form of Fire': ['Level 6. Become fire: fire immunity, pass through creatures (2d6 fire), burn melee attackers for 2d6, 30 ft line for 6d6, and maximize one fire die per turn.',
                  "You shed bright light 30 ft and dim light 30 ft further. You are immune to fire damage. You move through other creatures' spaces and ignore difficult terrain, and the first "
                  'creature you enter on your turn takes 2d6 fire. A creature within 5 ft that hits you with a melee attack takes 2d6 fire. As an action you make a line of fire 30 ft long and 5 ft '
                  'wide: each creature in it makes a Dexterity save, taking 6d6 fire on a failure or half on a success. On your turn, when you roll fire damage you can maximize one of the dice.'],
 'Form of Ice': ['Level 6. Become ice: cold immunity, icy ground in a 15 ft radius, 30 ft cone for 4d8 cold and half speed, and gain temporary HP from cold dice.',
                 'You are immune to cold damage and move across ice and snow difficult terrain freely. Ground within 15 ft of you is icy difficult terrain for everyone but you, and the radius moves '
                 'with you. As an action you make a 30 ft cone of freezing wind: each creature makes a Constitution save, taking 4d8 cold on a failure or half on a success, and on a failure its '
                 'speed is halved until the start of your next turn. On your turn, when you roll cold damage, you gain temporary hit points equal to one of the dice (your choice).'],
 'Form of Stone': ['Level 6. Become stone: resist nonmagical weapon damage, move through earth and stone, and raise spikes in 15 ft for 4d8 piercing.',
                   'You resist bludgeoning, piercing and slashing from nonmagical attacks. You cross earth and stone difficult terrain freely, and can move through solid earth or stone as if air '
                   'without disturbing it, but cannot end movement inside it. If you do, you are ejected to the nearest open space, the spell ends, and you are stunned until the end of your next '
                   'turn. As an action you raise stone spikes: creatures of your choice within 15 ft make a Dexterity save, taking 4d8 piercing on a failure or half on a success, and their space '
                   'becomes difficult terrain either way.'],
 'Form of Water': ['Level 6. Become water: resist nonmagical weapon damage, pass through creatures (Str save or prone), and a 15 ft line for 5d6 bludgeoning.',
                   "You resist bludgeoning, piercing and slashing from nonmagical attacks. You move through other creatures' spaces and ignore difficult terrain. The first time you pass through a "
                   'Large or smaller creature, it makes a Strength save or is knocked prone. As an action you unleash a blast of water 15 ft long and 5 ft wide: each creature in the line makes a '
                   'Strength save, taking 5d6 bludgeoning and falling prone on a failure, or half and not prone on a success.'],
 'Form of Wind': ['Level 6. Become wind: fly 60, move through creatures, invisible, and a 30 ft cone for 4d8 bludgeoning and a 15 ft knockback.',
                  "You gain a flying speed of 60 ft, move through and occupy other creatures' spaces, ignore difficult terrain and are invisible. As an action you unleash a 30 ft cone of wind: each "
                  'creature makes a Strength save, taking 4d8 bludgeoning and being knocked 15 ft away from you on a failure, or half damage and no knockback on a success.'],
 'Fortune': ['Level 2. Reaction. The triggering creature rerolls its d20 and uses the higher result.',
             'You reshape causality for the triggering creature in its favor. It must reroll the d20 and use the higher roll.'],
 'Frost Shuriken': ['Level 1. Ranged spell attack: 1d4 piercing and 2d8 cold. It bursts either way: adjacent creatures make a Dex save or take 2d8 cold.',
                    'You throw a bladed disk of ice at one creature in range with a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d4 piercing and 2d8 cold damage. The shuriken then explodes, hit '
                    'or miss. Each other creature within 5 ft of the target makes a Dexterity save or takes 2d8 cold. Higher slots: +1d8 cold per slot level above 1st.'],
 'Ghost Lights': ['Cantrip. Up to four small lights hover for 10 minutes, dim light 15 ft each. Move or douse them with a bonus action.',
                  'Create up to four small lights in range, each shaped and colored as you wish (torch, lantern, orb) and shedding dim light in a 15 ft radius. As a bonus action you can extinguish '
                  "or move any of them up to 60 ft. Each must stay within 30 ft of another, and one that exceeds the spell's range goes out. Casting the spell again extinguishes the earlier lights."],
 'Ghost Touch': ['Cantrip. Ranged spell attack: 1d8 necrotic and no healing until your next turn. Undead hit have disadvantage against you.',
                 'A cadaverous intangible hand grips a creature in range. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d8 necrotic damage and cannot regain hit points until the start of '
                 'your next turn. A hit undead has disadvantage on attack rolls against you until the end of your next turn. Damage rises to 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at 11 and 4d8 at 17.'],
 'Glacial Orbs': ['Level 6. Five frozen orbs to hold, hand off, throw 60 ft, or sling. Each bursts in 15 ft: Dex save, 3d8 cold and half speed.',
                  'Five bitterly cold balls appear in your hand. A creature can hold one, hand it to another, throw it up to 60 ft, or use it as ammunition for a sling or suitable weapon. A ball '
                  'shatters on impact and explodes in a 15 ft radius. Each creature there makes a Dexterity save, taking 3d8 cold and having its speed halved until the end of its next turn on a '
                  'failure, or half damage and no other effect on a success. Unused orbs evaporate when the spell ends. Higher slots: +1 ball per slot level above 6th.'],
 'Glyph of Power': ['Level 7. Casting 1 minute. A 5 ft hidden glyph that triggers a 60 ft effect: weakness, binding, death, bafflement, rage or stupor. Lasts until dispelled.',
                    'You mark a fixed surface with a 5 ft diameter inscription. It triggers when a creature enters its space or disturbs it. You can specify or exempt creatures or types, or set a '
                    'password a creature can speak as a reaction to prevent triggering. It is nearly invisible: finding it takes an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC, '
                    'with advantage for those who perceive magic (for example through detect magic). A creature can destroy it with an action, or the spell ends if the surface is destroyed, without '
                    'triggering. Choose one effect, spending its gem. When triggered the glyph flares and affects every non-exempt creature within 60 ft. Weakness (amethyst): Strength save or for 1 '
                    'hour speed 15 and weapon attacks deal minimum damage. Binding (topaz): Dexterity save or restrained 1 hour. Death (black sapphire): Constitution save or drop to 0 hit points, on '
                    'a success 10d8 necrotic. Bafflement (citrine): Intelligence save or for 1 hour cannot cast spells and has disadvantage on ability checks and attacks. Rage (garnet): Wisdom save '
                    'or hostile to all others and attacks the nearest, repeating the save each turn. Stupor (emerald): Charisma save or takes no actions with half speed, until 1 hour passes or it '
                    'takes damage.'],
 'Grave Call': ['Cantrip. Wisdom save or 1d8 necrotic (1d12 if below half HP).',
                'You chant a brief dirge at a creature in range, hastening its doom. It makes a Wisdom save or takes 1d8 necrotic damage, or 1d12 if it is below half its maximum hit points. Damage '
                'rises by one die at level 5, 11 and 17 (2d8 or 2d12, 3d8 or 3d12, 4d8 or 4d12).'],
 'Great Wave': ['Level 8. A 50 ft long, 50 ft high, 10 ft thick wave that crashes (6d10) and rolls 50 ft each turn, shrinking. Casting time can grow up to 6 rounds for a bigger wall.',
                'Summon a wall of water 50 ft long, 50 ft high and 10 ft thick at a point you see. You can lengthen casting up to 6 rounds, each adding 50 ft length and height and 10 ft thickness, '
                'to a maximum 300 by 300 by 60 ft. When it appears, each creature in the area makes a Strength save, taking 6d10 bludgeoning on a failure or half on a success. At the start of each '
                'of your turns afterward, the wall and any creatures in it move 50 ft along the ground in a direction you choose. A Huge or smaller creature inside it or whose space it enters makes '
                "a Strength save or takes 5d10 bludgeoning, only once per round. At the end of each turn the wall's height drops by 50 ft and later damage drops by 1d10. At 0 height the spell ends. "
                'A creature caught in the wall can swim out with a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC, otherwise it cannot move. A creature that leaves the area falls to the '
                'ground.'],
 'Hailstorm': ['Level 4. A 20 ft radius, 40 ft tall hail cylinder within 300 ft: difficult terrain, Dex save each turn for 5d4 bludgeoning + 5d4 cold.',
               'Balls of ice slam down in a 20 ft radius, 40 ft high cylinder centered on a point in range. The area becomes difficult terrain. A creature that starts its turn in the cylinder makes '
               'a Dexterity save, taking 5d4 bludgeoning and 5d4 cold on a failure or half on a success. Higher slots: both damages +1d4 per slot level above 4th, and radius and height +5 ft per '
               'slot level above 4th.'],
 'Hallucination': ['Level 2. A phantasm under 10 ft only the target perceives. It cannot hurt or impose conditions. Investigation vs your DC ends it.',
                   'You afflict a creature you see in range with an illusory phantasm of an object, creature or phenomenon you specify. It lasts the duration, is smaller than a 10 ft cube and only '
                   'the target perceives it, including sound and smell. It does not work on undead or constructs and cannot cause damage or conditions. The target acts as if it is real, and can '
                   'inspect it as an action with an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC (advantage if close enough to touch). Success ends the spell. As a bonus action '
                   'while in range you can adjust the phantasm, for example move a creature up to 30 ft, open a door or shatter a window.'],
 'Holy Fire': ['Level 5. A 10 ft radius, 40 ft tall column. Dex save: 8d8 radiant, fire, or half of each. Cover gives no benefit.',
               'Holy fire falls on all creatures in a cylinder 40 ft high and 10 ft in radius. Choose radiant, fire or both. Each creature makes a Dexterity save, taking 8d8 of the chosen type (4d8 '
               'of each if both) on a failure or half on a success. Cover gives no benefit on this save. Higher slots: +2d8 (or +1d8 of each type) for every two slot levels above 5th.'],
 'Imbue Element': ['Level 3. A touched melee weapon deals 1d6 bonus damage and acid, cold, fire or lightning as its base type, with a once-per-round rider.',
                   'Choose acid, cold, fire or lightning. For the duration the weapon deals 1d6 bonus damage on a hit and its base damage becomes that type. Once per round after a creature takes '
                   'damage from the weapon, a rider applies. Acid: the target takes 2d4 acid at the end of its next turn. Cold: its speed is halved until the end of its next turn. Fire: it takes 1d6 '
                   'more fire. Lightning: it cannot take reactions until the end of its next turn. Higher slots: bonus damage +1d6 for every two slot levels above 3rd.'],
 'Impaling Spires': ['Level 6. Raise up to six 30 ft rock spikes within 120 ft. Dex save: 5d10 piercing and impaled (restrained) if Large or smaller.',
                     'Up to six spikes of rock burst from the ground at places you see in range. Each fills a 5 ft space, is up to 30 ft tall, and has AC 11 and 30 hit points. A creature above a '
                     'spike when cast makes a Dexterity save, taking 5d10 piercing and, if Large or smaller, becoming impaled and restrained atop it on a failure, or half damage and nothing else on '
                     'a success. Huge creatures need two or more spikes to be restrained, Gargantuan need six or more. A creature in several spikes is damaged once. An impaled creature uses its '
                     'action for a Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check against your spell save DC, freeing itself and falling on a success, or is freed if all its spikes are '
                     'destroyed. If it is slammed into a ceiling or obstacle it takes 2d10 extra bludgeoning, and checks to free itself have disadvantage. The spikes crumble after 1 hour. Higher '
                     'slots: two more spikes per slot level above 6th.'],
 'Incinerate': ['Level 5. Wreathe a creature in flame: Dex save at the start of each turn for 10d6 fire (success halves and ends it). You can spread it. Killed targets turn to ash.',
                'A creature you see in range burns. At the start of each of its turns it makes a Dexterity save, taking 10d6 fire on a failure, or half and the spell ends for it on a success. A '
                'burning target sheds bright light 30 ft and dim light 30 ft further. As a bonus action you can spread the flames from a target to another creature within 10 ft of it, making that '
                'creature a target too. A target reduced to 0 hit points by the spell is turned to ash.'],
 'Inflict Disease': ['Level 5. Melee spell attack inflicts a magical disease: three Constitution saves decide cure or onset (7 days). Choose from six diseases with ability penalties.',
                     'Make a melee spell attack against a creature in reach. On a hit it is afflicted with a disease of your choice. It has no effect on constructs, undead or creatures immune to '
                     'disease. The disease is magical and cured only by heal or equivalent magic. At the end of each of its turns the target makes a Constitution save. On a success it suffers no '
                     'effects until the end of its next turn. Three successes end the disease. Three failures make it set in for 7 days or until properly treated. After three of either, it stops '
                     'saving. Muscle Weakness: disadvantage on Strength checks and saves and Strength attacks, which deal half damage. Trembling Spasms: the same for Dexterity. Skinslough: '
                     'disadvantage on Constitution checks and saves (except for this spell), and taking damage cuts its speed to 10 ft until the end of its next turn. Mindrot: disadvantage on '
                     'Intelligence checks and saves, and it cannot tell friend from foe. Fire-eyes Fever: disadvantage on Wisdom checks and saves, and blinded. Flesh Rot: disadvantage on Charisma '
                     'checks and saves, and it takes 5 extra damage from bludgeoning, piercing or slashing.'],
 'Injunction': ['Level 5. Casting 1 minute. Wisdom save or charmed 30 days and bound to obey: breaking your orders cuts current and maximum HP by 5d10 once per turn.',
                'You bind a creature in range that understands you to do or avoid an activity. It makes a Wisdom save or is charmed for the duration. Once per turn while charmed, if its behavior '
                'contradicts your instructions, its current and maximum hit points are reduced by 5d10 until the spell ends. You can give any command, but the spell ends if you order something '
                "suicidal. The creature's death does not end it. You can end it early with an action. Remove curse cast at its level also ends it. Greater restoration removes the maximum hit point "
                'reduction but not the spell. Higher slots: +1d10 maximum HP reduction per slot level above 5th. Slots 7 and 8 last 1 year. Slot 9 lasts until ended by one of those spells.'],
 'Irradiate': ['Level 4. A 30 ft sphere of blue light. On entering or starting a turn there, Con save or lose 7d4 max HP, 5 ft speed, and -2 to rolls. Five fails kills.',
               'A pulsing blue light fills a 30 ft radius sphere at a point in range, bright light that spreads around corners. When a creature first moves into the area on a turn or starts its turn '
               'there, it makes a Constitution save (constructs succeed automatically). On a failure its hit point maximum drops by 7d4, its speed drops by 5 ft, and it takes -2 on attack rolls, '
               'ability checks, saves and save DCs. Effects stack with each failure, and failing five times kills it. A failing creature also sheds light in a 5 ft radius and gets no benefit from '
               'invisibility, and each further failure adds 5 ft to the radius. All effects except death end when the spell ends. Higher slots: +1d4 max HP reduction per slot level above 4th.'],
 'Lashing Vine': ['Level 2. Casting 1 minute. A vine (AC and HP equal to your save DC) pulls a Large or smaller creature 20 ft on a failed Dex save, each turn as a bonus action.',
                  'A vine bursts from the ground, a wall or the ceiling in an open space you see in range. It is an object with AC and hit points equal to your spell save DC. When you cast and as a '
                  'bonus action on later turns you can direct it to pull a Large or smaller creature you see within 30 ft of it: the creature makes a Dexterity save or is pulled 20 ft straight '
                  'toward the vine. The spell ends if you cast it again or dismiss it as an action. Higher slots: range and pull distance +10 ft per slot level above 2nd, and slot 4+ can pull Huge '
                  'or smaller creatures.'],
 'Life Drain': ['Level 3. Up to three non-construct, non-undead creatures: ranged spell attack for 3d6 necrotic each, and you heal half the damage.',
                'Tendrils of necrotic energy suck life from up to three creatures in range that are not constructs or undead. Make a ranged spell attack against each, dealing 3d6 necrotic on a hit. '
                'You regain hit points equal to half the damage dealt. Higher slots: +1d6 for every two slot levels above 5th.'],
 'Lightning Beam': ['Level 3. A 100 ft by 5 ft lightning line that can bounce once off a non-conductive surface. Dex save: 4d12 lightning, half on success.',
                    'A beam of blue-white lightning leaps from your fingertips in a line 100 ft long and 5 ft wide. You can make it bounce once off a solid non-conductive object you see, such as a '
                    'stone wall, in a new direction you choose for its remaining length. Each creature in the path makes a Dexterity save, taking 4d12 lightning on a failure or half on a success. It '
                    'ignites unattended flammable objects in the area. Higher slots: +1d12 per slot level above 3rd.'],
 'Lightning Leash': ['Cantrip. Melee spell attack at 30 ft: 1d6 lightning and ensnared. If it moves out of range, yank as a reaction (Str save or 1d6 and half speed).',
                     "A crackling whip lashes at a creature you see within 30 ft. Make a melee spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d6 lightning and is ensnared. If it moves outside the spell's "
                     'range before the start of your next turn, you can use your reaction to yank the leash: it makes a Strength save or takes 1d6 lightning and has its speed halved until the start '
                     'of your next turn. Once it is out of range the leash fades. Both damage rolls rise by 1d6 at level 5, 11 and 17.'],
 'Lightning Tendril': ['Level 1. For 1 minute, use your action to zap a creature in 20 ft for 1d12 lightning. Higher slots add damage and range.',
                       'Crackling beams of blue energy leap from your hands. For the duration, as an action, you can direct them at a creature in range to deal 1d12 lightning damage. Higher slots: '
                       'slots 2 and 3 deal 2d12 with 30 ft range, slots 4 and 5 deal 3d12 with 60 ft, slot 6 or higher deals 4d12 with 120 ft.'],
 'Luminous Smite': ['Level 2. Bonus action. Next melee hit adds 2d8 radiant. The target cannot be invisible, ignores darkness cover, and sheds dim light 5 ft.',
                    'The next time you hit with a melee weapon attack before the spell ends, the weapon flashes with otherworldly light, dealing 2d8 extra radiant damage. Until the spell ends the '
                    'target cannot be invisible, is not obscured by a darkness spell, and sheds dim light in a 5 ft radius. Higher slots: +1d8 per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Lunar Beam': ['Level 2. A 5 ft radius, 40 ft tall beam of dim moonlight. Con save on entering or starting a turn: 2d10 radiant. Silver-vulnerable creatures do worse. Move it 60 ft each turn.',
                'A beam of moonlight shaped as a 5 ft radius, 40 ft high cylinder of dim light strikes a point in range. A creature that starts its turn in it or enters it on its turn makes a '
                'Constitution save, taking 2d10 radiant on a failure or half on a success. A shapechanger or creature vulnerable to silver has disadvantage, takes 1d10 extra on a failure, and cannot '
                'change form in the beam. As an action on later turns you can move the beam up to 60 ft in any direction within range. Higher slots: +1d10 per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Magic Fruit': ['Level 1. Infuse spell-component fruit for 24 hours: eating one restores 1 hit point, and ten feed a creature for a day.',
                 'You infuse the casting components with magic and the fruit gains minor healing properties for the duration. A creature can use its action to eat one fruit to restore 1 hit point. '
                 'Eating 10 infused fruits together gives enough nourishment for one day.'],
 'Magic Net': ['Level 1. Casting 1 minute. A hidden 5 ft radius, 10 ft high snare. Dex save or a creature is restrained and hoisted 10 ft up. Huge or larger succeed.',
               'You set a snare in a 5 ft radius, 10 ft high cylinder at a point on the ground in range. It is nearly invisible and can be found with an Intelligence check against your spell save '
               'DC. A creature that detects it is immune. A creature that moves in makes a Dexterity save or is restrained and lifted 10 ft up, hanging upside down. Huge and larger creatures '
               'automatically succeed. As an action a creature can free itself with a Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check against your spell save DC, ending the spell on a success.'],
 'Manipulate Earth': ['Cantrip. Shape earth in range: dig a 5 ft cube, make minor changes to dirt or stone, or make difficult terrain (up to three patches).',
                      'Choose one effect on earth you see in range. Excavate a 5 ft cube of loose dirt and move it along the ground to an open space within 5 ft. Make minor changes to dirt or stone, '
                      'such as changing color or carving small simple shapes. Turn a 5 ft square of earth or stone into difficult terrain for 1 hour, with up to three patches at once, the oldest '
                      'reverting if you make more.'],
 'Manipulate Fire': ["Cantrip. Control a fire in range: fire resistance for a creature until your next turn, spark or spread fire, douse a 5 ft cube, or change a flame's light, color or shape.",
                     'Choose one effect on a fire you see in range. Give a creature fire resistance until the start of your next turn. Spark or spread fire in a 5 ft cube if fuel is present. Douse '
                     "fire in a 5 ft cube. Adjust a flame's brightness (halve or double), color, or shape (simple forms) within a 5 ft cube for 10 minutes."],
 'Manipulate Water': ['Cantrip. Shape water in range: redirect a 5 ft cube, mold small shapes for 1 minute, recolor for 1 hour, or freeze or thaw a 5 ft cube.',
                      'Choose one effect on water you see in range. Move or direct a 5 ft cube of water, which returns to its natural flow at the start of your next turn unless you concentrate. Mold '
                      'it into small shapes or simple animations for 1 minute. Change its color or opacity in a 5 ft cube for 1 hour. Freeze up to a 5 ft cube of unoccupied water or thaw a 5 ft cube '
                      'of ice, which then melts or refreezes naturally (usually an hour or more).'],
 'Manipulate Wind': ['Cantrip. A small gust in range: disadvantage on the next ranged attack against a creature, push or knock prone a Large or smaller creature (Str save), +5 ft to a jump, or minor '
                     'effects.',
                     'Choose one effect. The next ranged weapon attack against a creature you choose in range has disadvantage. A Large or smaller creature you choose in range makes a Strength save '
                     'or is pushed 5 ft or knocked prone (your choice). Add 5 ft to the next jump of a creature you choose in range. Or manipulate the wind in a minor way, such as pushing a light '
                     'object up to 10 ft, rustling plants or slamming a door, never enough to move creatures or deal damage.'],
 'Martial Transformation': ['Level 6. 10 minutes. Gain 50 temporary HP, advantage on weapon attacks, +2d12 force, all armor and weapon proficiency, two attacks, and conjured gear, but no '
                            'spellcasting. Exhaustion risk after.',
                            'You take on the prowess of famed warriors. Until it ends you cannot cast spells or concentrate on them, and you gain: 50 temporary hit points; advantage on weapon '
                            'attacks and an extra 2d12 force damage on a hit; proficiency in all armor, shields, simple and martial weapons, and in Strength and Constitution saving throws; two '
                            'attacks with the Attack action unless you already have Extra Attack or similar; and you conjure and equip (as part of casting) any armor and any simple or martial '
                            'weapon, magical, with no Strength requirement, vanishing when the spell ends. Right after it ends you must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution save or gain one level of '
                            'exhaustion. You can end it as a bonus action.'],
 'Mass Freeze': ['Level 5. 20 ft radius within 60 ft. Con save: 4d8 cold, half on success. On a fail the creature is frozen: restrained, 1d8 cold each turn, repeat save.',
                 'Warmth vanishes around a point in range. Each creature in a 20 ft radius sphere makes a Constitution save, taking 4d8 cold on a failure or half on a success. A creature that fails '
                 'is frozen in place by sheets of ice, restrained and taking 1d8 cold at the start of each of its turns. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a '
                 'success.'],
 'Mind Link': ['Level 8. Link to a creature on any plane (Wisdom save, modified by distance and familiarity). Communicate, cast low divinations or illusions through it, and use its senses.',
               'You form a mental connection with another creature. It makes a Wisdom save modified by circumstance: on a different plane +10, secondhand knowledge +5, met in person 0, well known '
               '-5, within sight or hearing -5. It is aware of the contact and may choose to fail. On a failure you can communicate through the link and it recognizes you. You can also cast any '
               'divination or illusion spell of 4th level or lower that targets one creature on the linked creature regardless of range (such as detect thoughts or major image), affecting only it. '
               'As an action you can use its senses instead of yours until the start of your next turn. If you cast a spell this way, the target repeats its save at the end of each of its turns.'],
 'Minor Drain': ['Level 1. Ranged spell attack: 3d6 necrotic, and you gain half the damage as temporary HP for 1 minute.',
                 'A pulse of necrotic energy drains a target. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit it takes 3d6 necrotic damage and you gain half the damage dealt as temporary hit points, which fade '
                 'after 1 minute. Higher slots: +1d6 per slot level above 1st.'],
 'Misdirection': ['Level 5. Action or reaction when hit: become invisible and create an illusory double that mimics you. Creatures can see through it with Investigation.',
                  'As an action, or as a reaction when you are hit by an attack, you become invisible and hidden and create an illusory double in your space. The double moves at your speed, gestures '
                  'and speaks as you choose, and mimics your actions (your attacks and spells appear to come from it). It has your AC. Whenever a creature would damage the double or sees it attack '
                  'or cast, it makes an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC. On a success it knows the double is an illusion and you are no longer invisible to it. As an '
                  "action you can use the double's senses instead of yours until you use an action to return, or the spell ends. While you do, you are blinded and deafened to your own surroundings."],
 'Misfortune': ['Level 1. Reaction. The triggering creature rerolls its d20 and uses the lower roll.',
                'You reshape causality against the triggering creature. It must reroll the d20 and use the lower roll.'],
 'Morph Earth': ['Level 5. Reshape a 40 ft cube of earth into mud (4 ft of movement per foot, restraining) or into rock (AC 15, 25 HP) until dispelled.',
                 'Transform up to a 40 ft cube of earth. Create Mud: rock and dirt turn to mud for the duration. Creatures sink and each foot of movement costs 4 ft. A creature on the ground when '
                 'cast, entering for the first time, or ending its turn there makes a Strength save or is restrained. As an action, a restrained target or another creature within 5 ft ends the '
                 'restraint. Create Rock: wet earth less than 10 ft deep becomes rock. A creature standing in it when it hardens makes a Dexterity save: on a success it moves to an open space on the '
                 'surface, on a failure it is restrained. As an action, a restrained target or a creature within 5 ft can end the restraint with a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save '
                 'DC. The rock has AC 15 and 25 hit points and is immune to poison and psychic damage.'],
 'Muddy Servant': ['Level 2. A Medium mud golem (AC 12, 20 HP) grabs a creature (Str save: restrained, 2d6 bludgeoning) and squeezes on command for 2d6.',
                   'You mold loose soil and rock into a Medium mud golem in a 5 ft space in range. It has AC 12 and 20 hit points. It can immediately grab a Large or smaller creature within 5 ft: '
                   'Strength save or the target is restrained and takes 2d6 bludgeoning. While it is within 30 ft you can command it mentally as an action. If it is restraining a target you can '
                   'order it to squeeze: Strength save, 2d6 bludgeoning on a failure or half on a success. Or you can order it to dissolve and reform anywhere in range with full hit points (even if '
                   'destroyed) and try to grab a creature within 5 ft. You can order it to release a creature at any time without an action. A restrained target can use its action for a Strength '
                   '(Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check against your spell save DC to break free.'],
 "Nature's Fury": ['Level 5. All terrain within 60 ft is difficult for others. Each turn create trees (6d6 slashing), roots (restrain), a boulder (6d10), or a wind line (sweep 25 ft, prone).',
                   'All terrain within 60 ft of you is difficult terrain except for creatures you name. When you cast and as a bonus action on later turns, create one effect at a point you see '
                   'within 60 ft. Trees: a tree rakes foes. Each creature of your choice within 10 ft makes a Dexterity save or takes 6d6 slashing. Roots: roots seize creatures in a 10 ft radius, '
                   'Strength save or restrained. A creature within 5 ft of a restrained one uses an action for a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC to free it. Rocks: hurl a '
                   'boulder with a ranged spell attack for 6d10 bludgeoning, knocking Large or smaller targets prone. Wind: a gust in a line 60 ft long and 20 ft wide in a direction you choose. '
                   'Large or smaller creatures make a Strength save or are swept 25 ft and knocked prone.'],
 "Nature's Protection": ['Level 5. A 10 ft aura: three-quarters cover and difficult terrain for others. Bonus action or reaction: Str save or be pushed out (and prone on a failure).',
                         'The surrounding nature gives way for you and blocks others in a 10 ft aura that moves with you. The area gives three-quarters cover and is difficult terrain for creatures '
                         'other than you. As a bonus action, or as a reaction when a creature enters the aura, you make the elements surge outward. Large or smaller creatures in the aura make a '
                         'Strength save. On a success a creature is pushed out to the nearest open space, on a failure it is also knocked prone.'],
 'Necromantic Infusion': ['Level 3. A living target makes a Con save or takes 5d8 necrotic (half on success). An undead target gains 5d8 temporary HP and advantage on attacks.',
                          'You open a conduit to a plane of death and infuse a creature you see in range. A living target makes a Constitution save, taking 5d8 necrotic on a failure or half on a '
                          'success. An undead target gains 5d8 temporary hit points and, while it has them, advantage on its attacks.'],
 'Necromantic Storm': ['Level 5. A rift deals 6d8 necrotic (Con save half) within 10 ft to non-undead, spreading from kills (10 creatures max). Slain humanoids rise as zombies.',
                       'You tear a rift to a plane of death at a point in range. Non-undead creatures within 10 ft make a Constitution save, taking 6d8 necrotic on a failure or half on a success. If '
                       'the spell kills a creature, the blast spreads to a 10 ft radius around it. A creature cannot be damaged twice, and the spell ends after damaging 10 creatures. A humanoid '
                       "killed by it rises as a zombie at the start of your next turn and attacks the closest living creature (basic zombie or the reanimation template, other undead at the GM's "
                       'discretion). Higher slots: +2 creatures damaged per slot level above 5th.'],
 'Necrotic Sphere': ['Level 6. A 60 ft radius pulse drains up to eight creatures (fewest hit points first). Con save: 8d8 necrotic, half on success.',
                     'A pulse of necromantic power radiates in a 60 ft radius from a point you see in range, ripping life from up to eight creatures, starting at the center and moving outward, '
                     'prioritizing targets with fewer hit points. Each makes a Constitution save, taking 8d8 necrotic on a failure or half on a success. Higher slots: +4 creatures per slot level '
                     'above 6th.'],
 'Oakenhide': ['Level 2. Bark shell: gain 6 temporary HP at the start of each of your turns, and while you have them your AC is 15 + Dex (max +2).',
               'You encase yourself in bark. You gain 6 temporary hit points at the start of each of your turns, and while you have these temporary hit points you can calculate AC as 15 + your '
               'Dexterity modifier (maximum +2). Higher slots: AC +1 for every two slot levels above 2nd, and the temporary hit points rise by 3 per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Petrify': ['Level 6. Fleshy target makes a Con save: fail by 5+ is petrified at once, other failures are restrained and keep saving. Three successes end it, a failure petrifies.',
             'Choose a creature you see in range. If its body is flesh it makes a Constitution save. If it fails by 5 or more it is instantly petrified. Otherwise a creature that fails begins '
             'turning to stone and is restrained. A restrained creature makes another Constitution save at the end of each of its turns: three successes end the spell, and a failure petrifies it. '
             'Petrification lasts until greater restoration or similar magic frees it. A creature broken while petrified suffers the same damage if it returns to normal.'],
 'Phantasm': ['Level 2. Wisdom save or the target believes a phantasm: blinded, restrained, frightened, or taking 2d10 psychic each turn. Repeats save each turn.',
              "You plant a phantasm in a creature's mind. It makes a Wisdom save or believes it is real and able to hinder and harm it. Choose when you cast. Blinded: the phantasm blocks sight. "
              "Restrained: it entangles the target. Terrified: it takes the shape of the target's fears, making it frightened. Assailed: it is real enough to hurt, dealing 2d10 psychic at the start "
              "of each of the target's turns. The target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on a success."],
 'Phantasmal Horror': ['Level 4. A private nightmare. Wisdom save each turn: on a failure 4d10 psychic and frightened, on a success the spell ends.',
                       'Choose a creature you see in range. You create an illusion of its worst nightmares that only it can see. At the start of each of its turns it makes a Wisdom save. On a '
                       'failure it takes 4d10 psychic damage and is frightened. On a success the spell ends. Higher slots: +1d10 per slot level above 4th.'],
 'Phantasmal Nightmares': ['Level 9. Any creatures within 30 ft of a point: Wisdom save or frightened, taking 6d10 psychic each turn and suffering a d10 effect (dead-faint, paralysis, stun, no '
                           'speed, screaming).',
                           'Choose any number of creatures within 30 ft of a point you see in range. Each makes a Wisdom save or is frightened for the duration. At the start of each turn of a '
                           'frightened creature, it takes 6d10 psychic damage and rolls 1d10 for an effect lasting until the start of its next turn: 1 it believes itself dead and falls unconscious '
                           'until it takes damage or is woken as an action; 2-3 paralyzed with fear; 4-5 stunned; 6-7 speed 0; 8-10 screams uncontrollably and can make no other sound. A creature '
                           'repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell for itself on a success.'],
 'Poison Fang': ['Cantrip. A spectral snake bites a creature in 30 ft: Con save or 1d12 poison and poisoned until the start of its next turn.',
                 'A spectral snake bites one creature you see in range. It makes a Constitution save or takes 1d12 poison damage and is poisoned until the start of its next turn. Damage rises to '
                 '2d12 at level 5, 3d12 at 11 and 4d12 at 17.'],
 'Power Word Nap': ['Level 3. Up to three willing prone creatures sleep for one-fifth of a short rest and gain its benefit, once per long rest.',
                    'You command up to three willing prone creatures you see in range to sleep. The spell ends for a target that wakes, such as from damage or being shaken awake as an action. A '
                    'target that stays unconscious for the full duration gains the benefits of a short rest and cannot benefit from this spell again until it finishes a long rest. The duration is '
                    'one-fifth of a short rest (12 minutes for a one-hour rest). Higher slots: +1 willing creature per slot level above 3rd.'],
 'Prismatic Bolt': ['Level 1. Ranged spell attack: 1d8 decides the damage type and rider (acid, cold, fire, force, lightning, poison, psychic, thunder).',
                    'Make a ranged spell attack against one creature in range. On a hit the bolt deals 1d8 damage, and the number rolled sets the type and effect. If you roll more than one d8 (a '
                    'critical hit or higher slot), you choose which die decides. 1 Acid: 2d4 acid now and 3d4 acid at the end of its next turn. 2 Cold: 2d8 cold and speed halved until the end of its '
                    'next turn. 3 Fire: 3d6 fire. 4 Force: 3d4 force and prone if Large or smaller. 5 Lightning: 1d12 lightning and no reactions until the start of its next turn. 6 Poison: 1d12 '
                    'poison and poisoned until the end of its next turn. 7 Psychic: 2d8 psychic and charmed by you until the end of its next turn. 8 Thunder: 2d8 thunder and deafened until the end '
                    'of its next turn. Higher slots: the initial damage roll gains +1d8 per slot level above 1st.'],
 'Psychic Skewer': ['Level 2. Int save: 3d8 psychic. On a failure you pin its mind: bonus action to give -1d4 on its next save, and you always know where it is.',
                    'You pierce the mind of one creature you see in range. It makes an Intelligence save, taking 3d8 psychic on a failure or half on a success. On a failure you pin it and link to '
                    'its mind. For the duration you can use a bonus action to twist the skewer, making it subtract 1d4 from the next saving throw it makes before the end of your next turn. You also '
                    'know its exact location while you share a plane, it cannot hide from you and gains nothing from invisibility against you. If you concentrate for the full duration, this '
                    'knowledge lasts 1 hour after the spell ends. Higher slots: +1d8 per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Psychokinesis': ['Level 5. Move a Huge or smaller creature (Str save, can restrain it) or an object up to 1,000 lb by 30 ft. Hovers until your next turn. Continue each turn.',
                   'Creature: you try to move a Huge or smaller creature, yourself included. It makes a Strength save (it may fail willingly). On a failure you move it up to 30 ft in any direction '
                   'within range and may restrain it until the end of your next turn. Object: you try to move an object up to 1,000 lb with fine control. If unattended, you move it up to 30 ft in '
                   'range. If worn or carried, its holder makes a Strength save or you pull it away and move it up to 30 ft. A creature or object moved into the air hovers until the end of your next '
                   'turn. On each later turn you can use an action to continue (the target repeats the save) or pick a new target. You affect one creature or object at a time.'],
 'Rain of Fire': ['Level 7. A fire storm 20 to 300 ft above you. Call down 5 ft radius columns at five points within 120 ft: Dex save, 8d6 fire. Repeat as a bonus action.',
                  'A whirling firestorm forms at a height you choose between 20 and 300 ft above you, centered over your location. When you cast, and as a bonus action on later turns, you call down '
                  'a 5 ft radius cylinder of fire at five points you see within 120 ft. Creatures in an area make a Dexterity save, taking 8d6 fire on a failure or half on a success. A creature in '
                  'several areas is affected once. The fire ignites unattended flammable objects.'],
 'Reanimation': ['Level 3. Casting 1 minute. Raise a humanoid corpse (CR 2 or less) as a skeleton or zombie servant for 24 hours. Control up to your proficiency bonus in minions, total CR 3.',
                 'Choose bones or a corpse in range of a humanoid of CR 2 or lower. Bones become a skeleton, a corpse a zombie, by applying the template to its old stat block. On each of your turns '
                 'you can use a bonus action to command any or all minions you made with this spell within 60 ft, choosing an action and movement. Without orders a minion attacks hostiles or Dodges '
                 'if it senses none. Control lasts 24 hours, then the creature turns hostile to you and all living things. You can control a number of minions up to your proficiency bonus, with '
                 'total CR no higher than 3, and must wait 24 hours after making one before making another. Casting while you control servants can renew their duration instead. Skeleton template: '
                 'type Undead; Str 10, Dex 14 if lower; Con 15, Int 6, Wis 8, Cha 5; vulnerable to bludgeoning; immune to poison, exhaustion, poisoned; darkvision 60; HP at least 13; CR at least '
                 '1/4. Zombie template: Undead; Str 13 if lower, Dex 6 if higher; Con 16, Int 3, Wis 6, Cha 5; speed -10 ft; immune to poison and poisoned; darkvision 60; HP at least 22; CR at least '
                 '1/4; Undead Fortitude: at 0 HP, Con save DC 5 + damage taken (unless radiant or a critical hit) to drop to 1 HP instead. It keeps weapon and armor proficiencies, resistances, '
                 'immunities and natural attacks, loses languages but understands its creator. Higher slots: max CR and total CR +1 per slot level above 3rd. Slot 4+ allows beast corpses, slot 5+ '
                 'giants and monstrosities.'],
 'Reanimation, Greater': ['Level 3 base. Casting 1 minute. Raise a number of corpses up to your proficiency bonus (CR 6 or less) as skeletons, zombies or ghouls. Total CR 10, 24 hours.',
                          'Choose a number of bone piles or corpses in range up to your proficiency bonus, each of a creature of CR 6 or lower. Each rises as a skeleton, zombie or ghoul by applying '
                          'its template. On your turns you can use a bonus action to command any or all minions you made with this spell within 60 ft. Without orders a minion attacks hostiles or '
                          'Dodges. They are yours for 24 hours, then turn hostile to you and all living things. You control up to your proficiency bonus in minions with total CR no more than 10, '
                          'counting minions from reanimation. You can cast it with no targets to renew the control of all your current minions. Skeleton and zombie templates as in reanimation. Ghoul '
                          'template: Undead; Str 13 if lower, Dex 15 if lower; Con 10, Int 7, Wis 10, Cha 6; immune to poison, charmed, exhaustion, poisoned; darkvision 60; HP at least 22; CR at '
                          'least 1; gains a bite for 2d6 and a claw for 2d4 (Dex may replace Str). Once per turn a claw hit forces a DC 10 Constitution save or paralysis for 1 minute, repeating at '
                          'the end of each turn. Elves and undead are immune. Higher slots: max CR and total CR +1 per slot level above 3rd, beast corpses at slot 4+, giants and monstrosities at '
                          'slot 5+.'],
 'Rejuvenation': ['Level 7. Touch: the target heals 10 HP at the start of each turn for 10 minutes. Reaching your max HP knits scars and regrows lost limbs.',
                  'You imbue a creature with miraculous life. For the duration the target gains 10 hit points at the start of each of its turns. If you reach your hit point maximum while affected, '
                  'scars heal, missing limbs and digits regrow, and permanent wounds mend fully. The spell ends early if the target takes a single instance of fire or acid damage equal to or greater '
                  'than twice your level.'],
 'Riptide': ['Level 3. A 20 ft square wave within 60 ft. Str save: 4d8 bludgeoning, prone if Huge or smaller, and moved 15 ft on a failure.',
             'A sudden wave surges across a 20 ft square on the ground or in water you see in range. Each creature in it makes a Strength save. On a failure it takes 4d8 bludgeoning, is knocked '
             'prone if Huge or smaller, and is moved 15 ft in a direction you choose. On a success it takes half and is not knocked prone. Higher slots: +1d8 damage and +5 ft movement per slot level '
             'above 3rd.'],
 'Rot': ['Level 4. Con save: 9d8 necrotic and disadvantage on attacks and checks (half and no effect on success). Constructs and undead succeed, plants have disadvantage.',
         "Necrotic power blackens a creature's flesh. It makes a Constitution save. On a failure it takes 9d8 necrotic and has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks until the end of your "
         'next turn. On a success it takes half and nothing else. Constructs and undead succeed automatically, plants have disadvantage. Higher slots: +1d8 per slot level above 4th.'],
 'Sacred Circle': ['Level 5. A 60 ft radius, 120 ft tall cylinder: planar creatures have disadvantage attacking three chosen creatures. Action to lift charm, fear or possession. You allow or block '
                   'teleport and summoning.',
                   'A cylinder of resonating planar energy, 60 ft radius and 120 ft tall, forms on a ground point you see in range. Aberrations, celestials, elementals, fey, fiends and undead have '
                   'disadvantage on attack rolls against three creatures of your choice inside. As an action you can remove charm, fear or possession effects caused by such creatures from one '
                   'creature inside. You also choose whether to allow or block teleportation, planar travel and summoning within it.'],
 'Sacred Strikes': ['Level 1. Bonus action. For 10 minutes your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d6 radiant.',
                    'You ask for a divine blessing. For the duration your weapon attacks deal an extra 1d6 radiant damage.'],
 'Safekeeping': ['Level 7. Touch up to eight willing creatures or objects: hide each as invisible or an object of its size. Divination cannot find them. Creatures are incapacitated and do not age. '
                 'Ends on damage.',
                 'You hide up to 8 willing targets for the duration, turning each invisible or into an object of the same size such as a statue or portrait. Divination spells cannot locate or '
                 'perceive them. A hidden creature is incapacitated and does not age or need to breathe, eat or drink. The spell ends on a target if it takes any damage. You can also set a condition '
                 '(with GM approval) that ends it early.'],
 'Scintillant Blast': ['Level 7. A 60 ft cone of random magic: roll d8 per target for the type. Dex save, failure takes the full damage and rider, success half and nothing else.',
                       'A wave of force strikes everything in a 60 ft cone. Roll 1d8 for each target, which makes a Dexterity save, suffering the effect on a failure or half the initial damage and '
                       'no extra effect on a success. 1 Acid: 12d4 acid and another 12d4 at the end of its next turn. 2 Cold: 9d8 cold and restrained until the end of its next turn. 3 Fire: 14d6 '
                       'fire. 4 Lightning: 6d12 lightning, no reactions and disadvantage on Dexterity saves until the end of its next turn. 5 Poison: 6d12 poison and poisoned until the end of its '
                       'next turn. 6 Psychic: 9d8 psychic and stunned until the end of its next turn. 7 Thunder: 9d8 thunder, knocked back 30 ft and prone. 8 Multiple: struck by several blasts, roll '
                       'twice more, rerolling 8s.'],
 'Seal Away': ['Level 8. Casting 1 minute. Wisdom save or imprisoned forever: no aging, needs, or divination. You set a reasonable release condition. Dispel magic does not free it.',
               'You prepare a prison for a creature you see in range. It makes a Wisdom save or is imprisoned (on a success it is immune for 1 year). While imprisoned it does not age or need to eat, '
               'breathe or drink, and no divination can find it. You choose the prison form, such as a sealed demiplane, a gemstone or a cavity deep underground. You must specify a reasonable, '
               "possible condition that frees it (GM approval). It can involve a creature's name, identity or traits, but not game terms like level, class or hit points. Dispel magic cannot free it. "
               'If the condition occurs, the target is freed instantly.'],
 'Secret Missive': ['Level 1. Casting 1 minute. Write a hidden message that appears for 10 minutes when a chosen creature or password-speaker holds it. Lasts 10 days (more with costlier ink).',
                    'You write a secret message on parchment or paper. Choose a password or passphrase: when a creature speaks it while holding the page, the message shows for 10 minutes then fades. '
                    "Or name a creature, and it appears automatically in that creature's hands. Other text you write becomes invisible while the message shows. When the spell ends the message "
                    'vanishes forever. Truesight sees it. Dispel magic on the page ends the spell without revealing it. Duration depends on ink: magical ink worth 10 gp lasts 10 days, and each extra '
                    '1 gp adds a day. At 100 gp it is permanent.'],
 'Shape Winds': ['Level 5. Control a 300 ft cube of air for 1 hour: gale (extra cost against it, gusts), turbulence (disadvantage on ranged, half flight speed, Str save or prone), or thermal column '
                 '(reduce fall damage, triple jumps).',
                 'You seize air in a cube up to 300 ft on a side that you see in range. Choose an effect. It lasts until the spell ends or you use an action to pause or change it, and you can resume '
                 'a paused effect as an action. Gale: a steady wind in a horizontal direction you choose. Each foot of movement against it costs 2 extra feet, ranged attacks against the wind '
                 'automatically miss, and creatures moving with it gain 1 extra foot per foot spent. You can use your reaction to turn the wind when a creature or projectile moves in. As a bonus '
                 'action make a gust: creatures make a Strength save or are pushed 30 ft along the wind. Turbulence: a chaotic vortex. Ranged attacks through it have disadvantage. A creature flying '
                 'into it, starting its turn flying there, or taking flight there has its flying speed halved and makes a Strength save or is knocked prone. Thermal Column: wind blows upward. '
                 'Creatures taking fall damage in it reduce it by five times your spellcasting modifier, and vertical jumps there are tripled.'],
 'Shatter Mind': ['Level 8. 4d6 psychic and an Int save: on a failure Int and Cha become 1, it can only act by instinct. Repeat the save after a day, with growing delays.',
                  "You blast a creature's mind in range. It takes 4d6 psychic and makes an Intelligence save. On a failure its Intelligence and Charisma become 1. It can only take the most "
                  'instinctive actions, such as unarmed or natural attacks or running in a straight line. It cannot cast spells, activate magic items, understand language, use weapons or tools, or '
                  'communicate. It understands when another creature means it harm. After a day it can repeat the save, ending the spell on a success. Each failure adds one more day before the next '
                  'try. Greater restoration, heal or wish also end it.'],
 'Siphon Life': ['Level 3. Con save: a creature loses 4d8 HP (not reducible) and another creature within 30 ft of it regains the same. Willing creatures can fail. No effect on constructs and undead.',
                 'Choose one creature within 30 ft that you see. It makes a Constitution save. On a failure it loses 4d8 hit points, which cannot be reduced in any way, and another creature you '
                 'choose within 30 ft of the target regains the same amount. A creature can willingly fail. It has no effect on constructs or undead. Higher slots: +1d8 per slot level above 3rd.'],
 'Sky Omen': ['Level 6. A giant sky symbol visible 1 mile away for 1 hour. First sight: Wisdom save or terror (frightened) or awe (charmed). Courage grants advantage vs fear and charm. Higher slots '
              'widen radius and duration.',
              'You create a huge stationary symbol in the sky you see. You control its look, which can show animations up to 10 minutes long. It is visible in a 1 mile radius, plainly unnatural. The '
              'first time a creature sees it, it makes a Wisdom save (it may choose to fail if it reads the omen as positive). On a failure it suffers one effect, or another morale effect the GM '
              'decides. It can repeat the save at the end of each day. Terror: frightened of the omen. Awe: charmed and will not willingly go where it cannot see the omen. Courage: advantage on '
              'saves against fear and charm while it can see the omen. Higher slots: slot 7 gives 6 miles and concentration up to 8 hours, slot 8 gives 12 miles and up to 24 hours, slot 9 gives 18 '
              'miles, no concentration, until dispelled.'],
 'Sonic Rift': ['Level 3. Teleport 90 ft (with one willing creature) and the closing rift booms: creatures within 10 ft of start or end make a Con save or take 4d8 thunder.',
                'You step through a brief rift to an open space you see in range, bringing your gear and one willing creature your size or smaller that stands within 5 ft and appears within 5 ft of '
                'your destination (left behind if there is no room). The rift then closes with a sonic shockwave. Choose your starting or ending space. Creatures within 10 ft of it, except you and '
                'your companion, make a Constitution save, taking 4d8 thunder on a failure or half on a success. The boom is audible 300 ft away. Higher slots: +1d8 per slot level above 3rd.'],
 'Soul Transfer': ['Level 7. Casting 1 minute. Your soul enters a component and you try to possess a humanoid within 100 ft (Cha save). Trapped souls and death risks apply until dispelled.',
                   'Your body falls unconscious as your soul enters the material component. You perceive through it but cannot move or react. Your action lets you project your soul up to 100 ft, '
                   'either back to your body (ending the spell) or to try to possess a humanoid you see. Targets under protection from evil and good or circle of protection cannot be possessed. The '
                   'target makes a Charisma save. On a failure its soul is trapped in the component and you control its body, using its physical statistics but keeping your alignment and mental '
                   'scores (the GM decides which mental features apply). You can use an action to return to the component if within 100 ft, restoring the target. On a success you cannot try again '
                   'for 24 hours. The possessed creature perceives through the component and can repeat the save as an action after every hour, taking no other actions. On a success it returns to '
                   'its body and you return to the component if within 100 ft, otherwise you die. If the possessed body dies, the creature dies and you make a Charisma save against your spell save '
                   'DC to return to the component if within 100 ft, otherwise you die. If the spell ends or the container is destroyed, each soul tries to return to its living body within 100 ft, '
                   'otherwise it dies. Only wish prevents this death. The container is destroyed when the spell ends. Higher slots: slot 8 lets the target save once per day, slot 9 once per year.'],
 'Sparking Shot': ['Level 3. Bonus action. Charge ammo or a weapon: your attack arcs lightning, the target and two others within 15 ft make a Dex save or take 3d12 lightning. A hit auto-fails the '
                   "target's save.",
                   'You imbue a piece of ammunition or a weapon with electricity. When you attack with it, lightning arcs from the target. The target and two creatures of your choice within 15 ft '
                   'make a Dexterity save, taking 3d12 lightning on a failure or half on a success. If the attack hits, the target automatically fails. The item then returns to normal. Higher slots: '
                   '+1d12 per slot level above 3rd.'],
 'Speak with Nature': ['Level 1. Talk to beasts for 10 minutes. Slot 2+ lets you talk to plants, slot 3+ lets plants move and release or entangle.',
                       'You can speak with beasts for the duration. They can answer questions and tell you what they perceive or perceived in the past day, including nearby places and monsters. '
                       'Their knowledge and personality are limited by intelligence, and you can try to deceive, intimidate or persuade them as the GM decides. A creature need not answer, or answer '
                       'truthfully, if you are hostile or it sees you as an enemy. Higher slots: slot 2+ gives plants limited sentience so you can talk to them like beasts. Slot 3+ gives plants '
                       'limited movement: they can release a restrained creature, turn terrain into difficult terrain or back, or do other tasks the GM allows.'],
 'Spectral Champion': ['Level 3. Bonus action. A ghostly champion: choose cold, necrotic or radiant. Your weapon hits add 1d4 and stop healing. Each turn it attacks within 10 ft for 2d8 and Wis save '
                       'or speed 0.',
                       "A large incorporeal, invulnerable entity envelops you. Choose cold, necrotic or radiant: all the spell's damage is that type. Your weapons deal 1d4 extra damage on every hit, "
                       'and a creature taking it cannot regain hit points until the start of your next turn. When you cast and as a bonus action on later turns you can command the entity to make a '
                       'melee spell attack against a target within 10 ft. On a hit the target takes 2d8 and makes a Wisdom save or has its speed reduced to 0 until the end of its next turn. Higher '
                       'slots: +1d8 entity damage per slot level above 3rd.'],
 'Spell Glyph': ['Level 3. Casting 1 minute. A hidden 5 ft glyph stores a prepared spell of 3rd level or lower (1 action, targets another creature) that fires at whoever triggers it. Lasts until '
                 'dispelled.',
                 'You mark a fixed surface with a 5 ft diameter inscription. It triggers when a creature enters its space or disturbs it. You can refine the trigger by naming or exempting creatures '
                 'or types, or by setting a password a creature can speak as a reaction to prevent it. It is nearly invisible: an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC finds '
                 'it, with advantage for those who sense magic, as with detect magic. Destroying it with an action, or destroying the surface, ends the spell without triggering. During casting you '
                 'cast another prepared spell of 3rd level or lower into it. That spell must have a casting time of 1 action and be able to target a creature other than you. When it triggers it '
                 'releases the spell at the triggering creature. Area spells and summons center on that creature, and concentration spells last their full duration. A triggered glyph glows for the '
                 "stored spell's whole duration. Destroying it or its surface ends the spell. Higher slots: stored spell's max level +1 and material cost +50 gp per slot level above 3rd."],
 'Spirit Remnant': ['Level 3. Raise a spirit vestige from a corpse (not undead, not used in 10 days) to answer up to five questions in 10 minutes, honestly but cryptically.',
                    'You perform a rite over a corpse you see in range, summoning a vestige of its spirit to answer questions. The corpse needs a mouth or other way to speak, cannot be undead, and '
                    "cannot have been this spell's target in the last 10 days. For the duration it answers up to five questions using what it knew in life. Answers are typically brief, cryptic or "
                    'puzzling, but it neither lies nor refuses.'],
 'Spreadshot': ["Level 3. A 60 ft cone: one ranged attack roll with the weapon, every creature in the cone takes 4d8 on a hit or half on a miss, using the component's damage type.",
                'You touch the component and multiply the projectiles across a 60 ft cone. Make a single ranged attack roll with the weapon. Each target in the cone takes 4d8 damage on a hit or half '
                'on a miss. The type matches the weapon or ammunition used as the component. Higher slots: +1d8 per slot level above 3rd.'],
 'Stinging Insects': ['Cantrip. Insect cloud on a creature in 30 ft: Con save or 1d4 piercing + 1d4 poison and moved 5 ft (not into obvious danger).',
                      'A cloud of biting insects swarms a creature you see in range. It makes a Constitution save or takes 1d4 piercing and 1d4 poison and moves 5 ft in a direction you choose, never '
                      'into obviously dangerous ground such as fire or a pit. Both dice rise by one at level 5, 11 and 17 (2d4+2d4, 3d4+3d4, 4d4+4d4).'],
 'Stone Pact': ['Level 3. Touch rock for 1 hour: meld up to eight creatures into stone, gain 10 temporary HP and nonmagical resistance, or gain tremorsense 30 ft and immunity to prone and forced '
                'movement.',
                'You lay a hand on stone and ask for a boon. Choose one. Stone Meld: you and up to 7 other Large or smaller creatures you choose can meld with the stone. Until the end of your next '
                'round each willing creature can touch a 5 ft area and be absorbed. An absorbed creature sees and hears nothing but has tremorsense 30 ft, can exit as an action, and is ejected if '
                'the stone is destroyed or the spell ends. Stone Armor: stone covers your body, giving you 10 temporary hit points and resistance to nonmagical damage while you have them. Stone '
                'Step: you gain tremorsense 30 ft, and while standing on the ground you are immune to the prone condition and to being moved against your will.'],
 'Stormcloud': ['Level 4. A 20 ft radius, 100 ft tall storm, difficult terrain, lightly obscured, deafening. Bonus action lightning (2d12, ranged spell attack, advantage inside) then everyone inside '
                'makes a Con save for 4d8 thunder.',
                'A 20 ft radius cylinder of storms up to 100 ft high forms at a point in range. At the start of each turn you can move it up to 10 ft. It spreads around corners and is difficult '
                'terrain, lightly obscured, and creatures inside are deafened. As a bonus action each turn you direct a lightning strike at a creature within 60 ft of its center with a ranged spell '
                'attack, with advantage if the target is inside. On a hit it takes 2d12 lightning. After each strike every creature in the area makes a Constitution save, taking 4d8 thunder on a '
                'failure or half on a success. Higher slots: thunder +1d8 and lightning +1d12 for every two slot levels above 4th.'],
 'Stream of Flame': ['Level 2. A 30 ft by 5 ft line of fire. Dex save: 4d8 fire, half on success. Ignites unattended flammables.',
                     'A gout of flame shoots from your hand in a line 30 ft long and 5 ft wide. Each creature in it makes a Dexterity save, taking 4d8 fire on a failure or half on a success. It '
                     'ignites unattended flammable objects. Higher slots: +1d8 damage and +5 ft length per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Summon Animal Spirit': ['Level 2. Summon an Animal Spirit (Earth, Sea or Sky) for 1 hour. It shares your initiative and obeys your verbal commands.',
                          'You sculpt natural energy into a spirit animal in an open space you see in range, using the Animal Spirit stat block with an Earth, Sea or Sky option. It vanishes at 0 hit '
                          'points or when the spell ends. It is your ally, shares your initiative and acts right after you, and obeys your verbal commands. With no command it takes the Dodge action '
                          'and moves only to avoid hazards. Stat block (Medium beast, unaligned): AC 12 + spell level; HP 15 (Sky) or 25 (Earth, Sea) +5 per spell level above 2nd; speeds Earth 30 ft '
                          'and climb 30, Sea 10 and swim 30, Sky 15 and fly 60; Str 16, Dex 12, Con 16, Int 4, Wis 14, Cha 8; darkvision 60 ft, passive Perception 12; understands your languages; '
                          'uses your proficiency bonus. Traits: Flyby (Sky) no opportunity attacks when flying away; Pack Tactics (Earth) advantage near an ally that is not incapacitated; Blood in '
                          'the Water (Sea) advantage against creatures below max HP; Water Breathing (Sea). Multiattack: attacks equal to half the spell level, rounded down. Maul (Earth, Sea): your '
                          'spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft, 1d6+3 plus spell level piercing. Talons (Sky): your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft, 1d4+1 plus spell level slashing.'],
 'Summon Golem': ['Level 4. Summon a Golem Spirit (Flesh, Stone or Iron) for 1 hour. It shares your initiative and obeys your verbal commands.',
                  'You sculpt raw materials into a construct in an open space you see in range, using the Golem Spirit stat block with a Flesh, Stone or Iron option. It vanishes at 0 hit points or '
                  'when the spell ends. It is your ally, shares your initiative and acts right after you, and obeys your verbal commands. With no command it takes the Dodge action and moves only to '
                  'avoid hazards. Stat block (Medium construct): AC 11 + spell level (Flesh) or 13 + spell level (Iron, Stone); HP 50 +15 per spell level above 4th (Flesh) or 35 +10 per level (Iron, '
                  'Stone); speed 30 ft; Str 18, Dex 10, Con 16, Int 6, Wis 10, Cha 10; immune to charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned; Flesh also lightning immune, Iron '
                  'also fire immune; passive Perception 10; understands your languages; uses your proficiency bonus. Dissolving Rage (Flesh): below half HP at turn start it goes berserk with '
                  'advantage on attacks, losing 5 HP at turn end if it attacks nothing. Slowing Smash (Stone): once per turn on a hit, Wisdom save against your spell save DC or speed halved and no '
                  'reactions until the end of its next turn. Multiattack: attacks equal to half the spell level (only one can be Poisonous Gas). Slam: your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft, 1d8+4 '
                  'plus spell level bludgeoning. Poisonous Gas (Iron): creatures within 5 ft make a Constitution save against your DC or take 1d12 plus spell level poison and are poisoned until the '
                  'end of their next turn.'],
 'Summon Grave Spirit': ['Level 3. Summon a Grave Spirit (Ethereal, Ghoulish or Bone) for 1 hour. It shares your initiative and obeys your verbal commands.',
                         'You summon an undead creature in an open space you see in range, using the Grave Spirit stat block with an Ethereal, Ghoulish or Bone option. It vanishes at 0 hit points or '
                         'when the spell ends. It is your ally, shares your initiative and acts right after you, and obeys your verbal commands. With no command it takes the Dodge action and moves '
                         'only to avoid hazards. Stat block (Medium undead): AC 10 + spell level; HP 15 (Ethereal) or 25 (Ghoulish, Bone) +10 per spell level above 3rd; speed 30 ft (Ghoulish, Bone) '
                         'or fly 20 (Ethereal); Str 16, Dex 14, Con 14, Int 6, Wis 10, Cha 8; immune to necrotic, poison, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned; darkvision 60 ft, passive '
                         'Perception 11; understands your languages; uses your proficiency bonus. Ghostly Movement (Ethereal): moves through creatures and objects as difficult terrain, and if it '
                         'ends its turn inside an object it appears in the nearest open space and takes 1d10 force per 5 ft traveled. Terrifying Grasp (Ethereal): once per turn on a melee hit, '
                         'Wisdom save against your DC or frightened until the end of its next turn. Revive From Bones (Bone): when reduced to 0 HP by anything other than a critical hit or '
                         'bludgeoning, force or radiant damage, it leaves its bones, and you can revive it at 1 HP as a bonus action. Multiattack: attacks equal to half the spell level. Deathly '
                         'Chill (Ethereal): reach 5 ft, 1d4+2 plus spell level necrotic. Bone Arrow (Bone): range 80/320, 1d6+2 plus spell level piercing. Vile Claws (Ghoulish): reach 5 ft, 1d6+3 '
                         'plus spell level slashing, and Constitution save against your DC or poisoned until the end of its next turn, paralyzed instead if already poisoned. Attacks use your spell '
                         'attack modifier.'],
 'Symbol of Resilience': ['Level 3. A 30 ft hope aura you can move 30 ft as a bonus action. Allies gain advantage on Wisdom saves, boosted death saves, max healing, and a free Hit Die once each.',
                          'A tiny symbol above you radiates hope in a 30 ft radius, in any form you choose. As a bonus action you can move it up to 30 ft. Each non-hostile living creature in the '
                          'radius (including you) has advantage on Wisdom saves, adds your spellcasting modifier to death saves (treating 20 or higher as a natural 20), and regains the maximum hit '
                          'points possible from any healing. The first time a non-hostile living creature starts its turn in the radius, it can use a bonus action to spend one Hit Die and regain hit '
                          'points as with a short rest. If it was below half its maximum, it also gains temporary hit points equal to that amount until the spell ends. Higher slots: one extra Hit '
                          'Die per slot level above 3rd.'],
 'Synaptic Shockwave': ['Level 9. A 60 ft cone. Int save: 10d8 psychic and stunned (half and no effect on success). Stunned targets lose 1d6 Int each turn and save again with a bonus.',
                        'A wave of psionic energy fills a 60 ft cone. Each creature makes an Intelligence save, taking 10d8 psychic and becoming stunned on a failure, or half and no other effect on '
                        "a success. At the end of each of a stunned creature's turns it rolls 1d6 and its Intelligence drops by that amount. It then repeats the save using its original Intelligence, "
                        'adding the total Intelligence lost as a bonus. On a success it is no longer stunned. A creature reduced to Intelligence 0 dies. It regains 1 lost point after a long rest. '
                        'Heal, mass heal, regenerate and wish restore all of it instantly. Greater restoration restores 1d6 points.'],
 'Synaptic Spear': ['Level 4. Int save: 6d8 psychic and blinded and deafened until the end of your next turn (half and nothing else on success).',
                    'You hurl a spear of psychic energy at a creature in range. It makes an Intelligence save, taking 6d8 psychic and being blinded and deafened until the end of your next turn on a '
                    'failure, or half damage and no other effect on a success. Higher slots: +1d8 per slot level above 4th.'],
 'Tempest': ['Level 9. A storm cloud: 60 ft radius, up to 2,000 ft tall. Con save each turn or 4d8 thunder and deafened. Each action adds lightning, downpour, hurricane, hailstorm or expansion.',
             'You create a swirling storm cloud over a point you see, in a cylinder 60 ft in radius and up to 2,000 ft high. A creature starting its turn below the cloud makes a Constitution save or '
             'takes 4d8 thunder and is deafened until the start of its next turn. While you concentrate you can use an action to add an effect, which lasts for the duration. Earlier effects stay, '
             'and most can be added only once. Lightning: as a bonus action choose two points below the cloud. Creatures within 10 ft of either make a Dexterity save, taking 4d12 lightning on a '
             'failure or half on a success. Downpour: the entire area becomes difficult terrain and heavily obscured to everyone but you. Hurricane: ranged weapon attacks in the area automatically '
             'miss, and each Huge or smaller creature starting its turn below makes a Strength save or is thrown 30 ft in a random direction and knocked prone. Hailstorm: each creature below takes '
             '2d10 bludgeoning at the start of its turn, and creatures below have disadvantage on concentration saves. Expansion: move the storm 120 ft or add 60 ft to its radius, any number of '
             'times.'],
 'Thought Wisp': ['Cantrip. Turn a thought, memory or message into a Tiny wisp that lasts 24 hours. A chosen creature (or anyone) can use an action to receive it.',
                  'You touch your head and move a thought into a Tiny, weightless, semisolid wisp in your hand. Its color shows the thought: yellow for ideas, silver for memories, blue for messages. '
                  'When casting you can limit who may receive it to specific creatures or types. A specified creature can use an action to receive its contents, ending the spell. With no limit, any '
                  'creature can. A creature that can cast this spell, or is concentrating on a thought-reading spell like detect thoughts or modify memory, can use an action to receive its contents, '
                  'ending the spell. Such a creature can also cast this spell to turn thoughts it reads into a wisp. Modify memory can affect wisps. A creature can touch a wisp and use an action to '
                  'disperse it, ending the spell.'],
 'Thunder Burst': ['Cantrip. A boom audible 300 ft away: creatures within 5 ft make a Con save or take 1d8 thunder and are deafened until the end of their next turn.',
                   'You create a concussive pulse that booms out to 300 ft. Other creatures within 5 ft of you must succeed on a Constitution save or take 1d8 thunder damage and be deafened until '
                   'the end of their next turn. Damage rises to 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at 11 and 4d8 at 17.'],
 'Touch of Filth': ['Level 2. Melee spell attack each turn: 1d6 poison and poisoned. The target saves with Con at the end of each turn to end the poison.',
                    'Your hand is wreathed in vile miasma. Make a melee spell attack against a creature in reach. On a hit it takes 1d6 poison and is poisoned. At the end of each of its turns it can '
                    'make a Constitution save, ending the poison on a success. Until the spell ends you can repeat the attack on each of your turns as an action. Higher slots: +1d6 per slot level '
                    'above 2nd.'],
 'Twister': ['Level 7. A 30 ft radius, 100 ft tall tornado within 300 ft, movable 30 ft as an action. Str save when entering or starting a turn: 10d6 bludgeoning, and Large or smaller creatures are '
             'caught and carried up.',
             'A tornado fills a 30 ft radius, 100 ft high cylinder at a point on the ground in range. As an action you can move it up to 30 ft along the ground. A creature that enters it on its turn '
             'or starts its turn there makes a Strength save, taking 10d6 bludgeoning on a failure, and if Large or smaller it is sucked in and restrained. Restrained creatures move with the twister '
             'and are carried 25 ft up each round toward its center. At the end of each of its turns a restrained creature repeats the save, and on a success is hurled 60 ft horizontally in a random '
             'direction. The area is lightly obscured, and ranged attacks passing through it automatically miss.'],
 'Unbridled Fury': ['Level 2. Wisdom save or a humanoid is charmed with rage. You can trigger it: it must rush the nearest creature and make a melee attack. It repeats the save each turn.',
                    'You plant an unquenchable rage in a humanoid you see in range. It makes a Wisdom save or is charmed by you, its eyes glowing. When you cast, and as an action on later turns, you '
                    'can activate the rage: at the start of its turn the target must move up to its speed toward the nearest creature and use its action for one melee attack against it. If you do '
                    'not activate it, or it cannot reach anyone, it takes its turn normally. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on a success. Higher slots: at slot '
                    '4+ the target makes two melee attacks if it has multiple attacks.'],
 'Unearth Legend': ['Level 5. Casting 1 minute. Offer gems to an entity to research a person, place or object for up to 7 days. Results appear in a notebook, possibly as riddles.',
                    'You contact an otherworldly entity and offer it the casting gems in exchange for the history of a person, place or object. It tells you all it knows about the subject, typically '
                    'well-known lore. It then researches for up to seven days, and its discoveries appear as writing in the jeweled notebook, perhaps obscure myths, forgotten legends or lost '
                    'secrets. The more you already know when casting, the faster and more detailed the results. It may not understand what it finds and can give riddles, confusing poems or puzzling '
                    'messages. The spell ends once it has conveyed everything it can learn.'],
 'Unerring Sentry': ['Level 4. Casting 1 minute. An arcane sentry (Small or Medium, invisible to non-allies) sounds an alarm at CR 1/4+ creatures within 60 ft and attacks on command for 4d8 force.',
                     'You conjure an obviously magical, Small or Medium sentry in an open space in range. It lasts the duration, until you dismiss it, until you move 100 ft from it, or until you '
                     'cast the spell again. Designate any number of creatures you see as its allies. It is invisible to everyone else and calls an alarm if any other creature of CR 1/4 or higher '
                     'comes within 60 ft. It sees invisible creatures and into the Ethereal Plane and cannot be fooled by illusions. As an action on your turn you can direct it to attack a target '
                     'you see within 100 ft of its original location. It moves up to 30 ft and you make a melee spell attack against a creature within 5 ft, dealing 4d8 force on a hit. If you are '
                     'incapacitated, unconscious or cannot direct it, at the end of your turn it attacks the nearest creature of CR 1/4 or higher that is not its ally.'],
 'Wall of Dust': ['Level 3. A 30 by 10 by 10 ft wall of grit for 10 minutes. It blocks sight, blinds and deafens inside, and slows: 6 ft of movement per foot on a failed Str save, 3 ft on a success.',
                  'You build a wall of blowing dirt and grit up to 30 ft long, 10 ft high and 10 ft thick at a point in range. It blocks line of sight, and a creature inside is blinded and deafened. '
                  'When a creature enters or starts its turn in it, it makes a Strength save. On a failure each foot it moves through the wall costs 6 ft of movement, on a success 3 ft. The wall '
                  'vanishes when the spell ends.'],
 'Warding Sigil': ['Level 1. Bonus action. A ward with 4 HP and resistance to nonmagical weapon damage types takes your damage instead of you. Excess carries over and ends it.',
                   'You make a protective sign. The ward has 4 hit points and resists bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage. For the duration, whenever you take damage the ward takes it instead. '
                   'If this drops the ward to 0 hit points, you take any remaining damage and the spell ends. Higher slots: +2d4 ward hit points per slot level above 1st.'],
 'Water Wall': ['Level 3. A 30 by 10 by 5 ft wall (or a ring 15 ft across, 20 ft high) of water. Movement costs triple. Str save for 2d6 bludgeoning. Halves ranged damage with disadvantage and '
                'douses fire.',
                'You summon a wall of swirling water on the ground in range: up to 30 ft long, 10 ft high and 5 ft thick, or a ring up to 15 ft in diameter, 20 ft high and 5 ft thick. Each foot '
                'moved through it costs 3 ft of movement. A creature that starts its turn in it or enters it on its turn makes a Strength save, taking 2d6 bludgeoning on a failure or half on a '
                'success. Ranged attacks passing through have disadvantage and deal half damage. Fire effects passing through are extinguished. Cold effects affect any creature within 5 ft of the '
                'point they touch the wall. Lightning effects deal half their damage to any creature in contact with the wall.'],
 'Wayfinding': ['Level 5. Casting 1 minute. Learn the way to a named place on your plane for 24 hours. Pick dowsing (distance and direction), ascertainment (shortest route) or forecast (30 miles of '
                'hazards).',
                'You name a location on your plane and gain supernatural knowledge of the way there. If it moves to another plane the spell fails. Choose an option, lasting the duration, and you can '
                'end one with an action to take another. Dowsing: the pendulum tugs toward the goal with growing urgency, telling you distance and direction. Ascertainment: at any choice of paths '
                'the pendulum points to the shortest, most direct route, ignoring safety. Forecast: the mirror shows the next 30 miles on the path, giving general awareness of natural hazards like '
                'decaying bridges or cliffs.'],
 'Wellspring': ['Level 2. A 10 ft radius healing pool within 30 ft. Any time, restore 2d4 HP to a creature in it, then it recharges at the start of each of your turns.',
                'You pour out pure water and create a 10 ft radius magical pool on the ground in range. At any time, without an action, you can restore 2d4 hit points to any creature in the pool, '
                'depleting its magic. The magic returns at the start of each of your turns. Higher slots: healing +1d4 and radius +5 ft per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Whirling Blades': ['Level 2. A 5 ft sphere of metal shards deals 4d4 slashing on entry or turn start. As an action fire it at a creature within 30 ft (ranged spell attack, 4d4 piercing, half on '
                     'miss) and the spell ends.',
                     'You produce a storm of metal shards in a 5 ft diameter sphere in a space you see in range. A creature takes 4d4 slashing when it enters the area for the first time on a turn or '
                     'starts its turn there. As an action you can send the blades at a creature within 30 ft of the sphere with a ranged spell attack, dealing 4d4 piercing on a hit or half on a '
                     'miss. Either way the spell then ends. Higher slots: +2d4 per slot level above 2nd.'],
 'Whirling Water': ['Level 4. A 10 ft radius water sphere. Str save or restrained inside. Roll it 30 ft as an action, hurl a creature out for 4d6 as a bonus action, and put out fires.',
                    'A swirling ball of water fills a 10 ft radius at a point on the ground or in water in range. A creature that enters on its turn or starts its turn there makes a Strength save or '
                    'is restrained and trapped. It repeats the save at the start of each of its turns. A Huge or smaller creature partly inside has advantage, a Gargantuan creature succeeds '
                    'automatically. As an action you can roll the sphere up to 30 ft, carrying restrained creatures and dousing nonmagical flames it passes. If a creature inside collides with a '
                    'creature outside, both take 4d6 bludgeoning. Restrained creatures ignore terrain the sphere crosses. As a bonus action you can hurl a restrained creature 20 ft in a direction '
                    'you choose for 4d6 bludgeoning, and a creature it hits makes a Dexterity save or takes 4d6 bludgeoning. When it ends, restrained creatures fall prone and fires within 20 ft are '
                    'put out. The water then vanishes.'],
 'Whirlpool': ['Level 5. A 30 ft radius churning pool in range. Str save at turn start or entry: 5d8 bludgeoning and pulled 10 ft toward the center. +1d8 in an existing body of water.',
               'You conjure a 30 ft radius circle of churning water on the ground or in water you see in range. The area is difficult terrain but not deep enough to require swimming. A creature that '
               'starts its turn there or enters on its turn makes a Strength save, taking 5d8 bludgeoning and being pulled 10 ft toward the center on a failure. If it targets an existing body of '
               'water, damage is +1d8. Higher slots: +1d8 per slot level above 5th.'],
 'Withering Field': ['Level 8. A 30 ft cube in range. Con save: 12d8 necrotic, half speed and disadvantage on attacks and checks until your next turn (half and nothing else on success). Constructs '
                     'and undead succeed, plants have disadvantage. Kills crumble to dust.',
                     'You shrivel every living thing in a 30 ft cube you see in range. Each creature makes a Constitution save. On a failure it takes 12d8 necrotic, has its speed halved, and has '
                     'disadvantage on all attack rolls and ability checks until the end of its next turn. On a success it takes half and nothing else. Constructs and undead succeed automatically, '
                     'plants have disadvantage. Anything reduced to 0 hit points under the spell crumbles to dust.'],
 'Wound': ["Level 6. Con save: 14d6 necrotic (half on success), and the target's maximum HP drops for 1 hour by the necrotic damage taken.",
           'You send negative energy into a creature you see in range. It makes a Constitution save, taking 14d6 necrotic on a failure or half on a success. Its hit point maximum is reduced for 1 '
           'hour by the necrotic damage it took.']}
